&lt;p&gt;Also, don’t forget to follow &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/saas-group/&quot;&gt;saas.group on LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; to stay up-to-date on our job openings, podcast episodes, and with all things happening at our company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-33&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0&quot;&gt;We are looking for a hands-on, detail-oriented Managing Director to lead SaaS.group GmbH, our German legal entity based in Schönefeld&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2&quot;&gt;. In this role, you will serve as the registered Managing Director on-site, exercising real decision-making authority, managing office administration, and overseeing day-to-day accounting operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,4&quot;&gt;. You will serve as the local face of the company for authorities, banks, auditors, and external service providers while working in close alignment with our Central Legal, Accounting, and Finance teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,6&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;source-inline-chip-container luminous-sources hide-from-message-actions ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-34&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0&quot;&gt;This is a unique opportunity for an experienced finance or office management professional based in the Berlin/Brandenburg region looking to step up into an official corporate leadership role within an international, fast-growing software group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Your immediate impact in the first 3-6 months will be:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-35&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0&quot;&gt;Seamlessly transition into the registered Managing Director role for SaaS.group GmbH and establish effective on-site operational processes in Schönefeld&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2&quot;&gt;Assume complete oversight of local bookkeeping (payables, receivables, document management) and streamline month-end close workflows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4&quot;&gt;Build strong working relationships with our external tax advisors, auditors, banks, and internal group accounting/legal functions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,6&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,6&quot;&gt;Ensure full compliance with all corporate-law requirements, commercial register obligations, and internal rules of procedure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0&quot;&gt;Manage SaaS.group GmbH on-site in Schönefeld, taking full ownership of approvals, contract execution, and payment authorizations within defined rules of procedure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2&quot;&gt;Run and oversee day-to-day bookkeeping, including accounts payable/receivable, document organization, and preparation of month-end closing activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with tax advisors and auditors on VAT filings, annual financial statements, and audit processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,6&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,6&quot;&gt;Maintain strict compliance with German corporate-law obligations, including commercial register filings, transparency register updates, and shareholder resolutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,8&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,8&quot;&gt;Lead office management and operational setup in Schönefeld, managing incoming mail, vendor/service provider contracts, archiving, and filing systems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,10&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,10&quot;&gt;Act as the primary local point of contact for the German tax office (Finanzamt), financial institutions, local authorities, and insurers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,12&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You bring to the table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0&quot;&gt;Vocational training in a commercial field (e.g., Tax Clerk / Steuerfachangestellte/r, Certified Accountant / Bilanzbuchhalter/in, Office Management) or equivalent practical experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2&quot;&gt;Multi-year background in accounting, financial administration, or senior office management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,4&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,4&quot;&gt;Strong proficiency with DATEV (or comparable accounting software) as well as modern digital tools (MS Office / Google Workspace)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,6&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,6&quot;&gt;Fluency in German and good working proficiency in English to collaborate effectively across our international group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,8&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,8&quot;&gt;Willingness to assume corporate liability and responsibility as a registered Managing Director (leadership experience is a plus, but not required)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,10&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,10&quot;&gt;Residence in the Berlin/Brandenburg region with the requirement for regular, physical presence at our Schönefeld office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,12&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s in it for You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Real Responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-5175 citation-end-5175&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;A genuine Managing Director role with clear rules of procedure, corporate protection (D&amp;amp;O insurance included), and direct collaboration with the group CFO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-5174 citation-end-5174&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Freedom and autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; We’re a high-trust team, and you’ll be given lots of flexibility to solve problems in your own way — with plenty of help from the team when you need it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum bureaucracy:&lt;/strong&gt; We don’t like to get bogged down with meetings and red tape. We like to be efficient and keep momentum steady &amp;amp; sustainable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Small &amp;amp; friendly team:&lt;/strong&gt; We help each other out, have fun, and joke around.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our network:&lt;/strong&gt; We are a community of entrepreneurial SaaS professionals that regularly exchange ideas, knowledge, learning&amp;nbsp; and expertise with each other internally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible time off:&lt;/strong&gt; We want you to recharge your batteries when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t just simply offer you to “take a job with us” but rather to “join us on this journey” &lt;em&gt;to build the world&#39;s largest platform of independent SaaS companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sounds like something you’re up for? Feel free to apply even if you don’t check all these boxes. We believe in the power of diversity and fresh perspectives to spice up our team. Your application might just be the missing ingredient!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;saas.group is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. If you&#39;re passionate about working with a team that values innovation, excellence, and fairness, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe in fair and transparent pay. Salary ranges at saas.group are location-adjusted, targeting local market medians for a remote-first environment, and will be shared with our potential future employees in writing before your first interview - so you have everything you need to evaluate the opportunity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/saasgroup/managing-director-focus-on-accounting-office-schonefeld-288577","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":[],"location":"Schönefeld","created_at":1792227318},{"slug":"solutions-engineer-uas-aviation-munich-114919","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Solutions Engineer UAS / Aviation","description":"&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Solutions Engineer UAS / Aviation who will play a pivotal role in the future of our company. Our Solutions Engineer will be responsible for the integration, validation, and operational readiness of Auterion-powered drone systems. You’ll collaborate closely with the production team, as well hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, and operations while ensuring that every platform transitions successfully from a physical airframe into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. This role is ideal for someone who lives and breathes drone technology and enjoys bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 and/or other autopilot&amp;nbsp; ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute End-of-Line (EoL) software validation and functional testing to ensure production readiness and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct payload and camera load-seat testing, validating integration stability and operational performance under real-world conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot embedded system issues spanning firmware, communication interfaces, sensors, and hardware-software interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to diagnose integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating closely with engineering and manufacturing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to validation workflows for complete UAV systems, including components, integrated features, and operational flight configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support full-stack drone integration activities across hardware, embedded firmware, and flight software layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex integration and reliability challenges involving sensors, flight controllers, communication protocols, and power systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable impact on product quality, manufacturing throughput, and deployment readiness through improved validation and testing processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to accelerate batch validation and reduce EoL cycle times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with external vendors and equipment providers to support testing infrastructure, hardware integration, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in hands-on flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc. in Aviation Technology, Robotics, Embedded Systems, Electrical Engineering, or related field (M.Sc. optional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with Autopilot, Mission planning and navigation Software, including firmware flashing, configuration, and flight validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical foundation in embedded systems, firmware debugging, and hardware-software integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in C/C++ and/or MAVLink communication protocols or equivalent Datalink protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UAV sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and flight controller configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Linux-based development and debugging environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UAV flight testing, system validation, and troubleshooting in real-world operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of drone manufacturing, QC processes, and End-of-Line testing methodologies is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills when working with cross-functional engineering and operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently in fast-paced environments with evolving technical challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for drone technology and a hands-on engineering mindset focused on building reliable flying systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/auterion/solutions-engineer-uas-aviation-munich-114919","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792227318},{"slug":"growth-associate-intern-berlin-16164","company_name":"Melotech","title":"Growth Associate (Intern)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech is revolutionizing media and entertainment. We create art through technology for humans to enjoy. In just 24 months, our work has been heard, watched and loved for over 4 billion minutes worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by entrepreneur and investor Soheil Mirpour, we are backed by top VCs Cherry Ventures, Speedinvest and GFC, alongside world-class angels from firms such as Spotify, Blackstone and KKR.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech is scaling fast, and organic reach is one of the engines behind it. As Growth Associate (Intern), you help run that engine end to end: the creators, the formats, the trends and the numbers behind them. This is an organic growth role first, measured on how much reach every hour and every euro brings back. You work directly with our founders, our Growth Manager, product and data team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today that means a steady stream of new products that each deserve a shot at going viral across TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Your first job is to build the machine behind that: find the creators and communities that move culture, turn what works into repeatable playbooks, and run more experiments in a week than most teams run in a quarter.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">On a typical day, your tasks may include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creator network:</strong> finding, briefing and paying creators and pages at scale, from small accounts with loyal audiences to the ones that set trends, and keeping the ones that deliver</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Seeding:</strong> getting our products into the formats and communities where they can travel, at the right moment and in the right volume</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trend spotting:</strong> catching formats and memes early and moving on them within days, not weeks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experiments:</strong> running many cheap tests every week, with clear rules for what wins and what gets killed, and turning the winners into playbooks the team can repeat</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>New channels:</strong> finding places where attention is still cheap, from fan pages and communities to platforms nobody on the team is using yet</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organic and paid together:</strong> working with our Growth Manager so organic winners get scaled with paid, and what paid learns feeds back into organic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement:</strong> knowing which number answers which question, for example what saves and shares tell you that views do not, and what each view really costs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling:</strong> building the trackers, scripts and automations you need, with platform data and AI tools as your daily coworkers</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a student or recent graduate who lives on the platforms and wants to learn how to make content travel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically, your profile will look like this:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform fluency:</strong> you know TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts well and can explain why a post performs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on experience:</strong> you have grown an account, a page or a side project, or supported a startup or brand on social</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creator marketing:</strong> you enjoy working with creators and have a feel for content that looks native</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creativity:</strong> you bring fresh ideas and test them in a structured way</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical:</strong> you are comfortable with numbers and spreadsheets; SQL, Python or AI tools are a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pace:</strong> you thrive in a fast-paced and performance-oriented environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A big plus:</strong> you are a creator yourself, or have run pages with a real following</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academics:</strong> pursuing or recently graduated with a degree at a top-tier university, with an outstanding academic record: grades, scholarships or awards to show for it</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes this exciting</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own a lever the whole company feels. Every breakout you engineer shows up directly in how fast we can grow, at a fraction of what paid reach would cost. You're not a cog in the machine but the captain of your own ship, rewarded for performance and respected for leadership. Flat hierarchies mean that your voice matters, your ideas get implemented, and your impact is immediate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We pay competitive salaries and make you an owner of the business with equity. We work remotely to give you complete freedom over your life, while meeting regularly around the world for global offsites where we strategize, bond, and push boundaries together.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What the process will look like</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire on a rolling basis. Earliest starting date is always ASAP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Once you begin our process, you can progress from start to offer within a week, depending on how quickly you can move through each stage:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview: 30-minute introductory call, getting to know you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case interview: 90-minute case discussion, present and debate your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder interview: 90-minute interview with our CEO, going deep on all topics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, contract signing and onboarding</p></li></ol><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Note: As we are still in stealth, you will learn more about Melotech as you progress through the stages. By the end of the Founder interview, you will have a full grasp of our business and the details of your role.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/melotech/growth-associate-intern-berlin-16164","tags":["Marketing & Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792226419},{"slug":"organic-growth-lead-berlin-122857","company_name":"Melotech","title":"Organic Growth Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech is revolutionizing media and entertainment. We create art through technology for humans to enjoy. In just 24 months, our work has been heard, watched and loved for over 4 billion minutes worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by entrepreneur and investor Soheil Mirpour, we are backed by top VCs Cherry Ventures, Speedinvest and GFC, alongside world-class angels from firms such as Spotify, Blackstone and KKR.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech is scaling fast, and organic reach is one of the engines behind it. As Organic Growth Lead, you own that engine end to end: the creators, the formats, the trends and the numbers behind them. This is an organic growth role first, measured on how much reach every hour and every euro brings back. You work directly with our founders, our Growth Manager, product and data team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today that means a steady stream of new products that each deserve a shot at going viral across TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Your first job is to build the machine behind that: find the creators and communities that move culture, turn what works into repeatable playbooks, and run more experiments in a week than most teams run in a quarter.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">On a typical day, your tasks may include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creator network:</strong> finding, briefing and paying creators and pages at scale, from small accounts with loyal audiences to the ones that set trends, and keeping the ones that deliver</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Seeding:</strong> getting our products into the formats and communities where they can travel, at the right moment and in the right volume</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trend spotting:</strong> catching formats and memes early and moving on them within days, not weeks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experiments:</strong> running many cheap tests every week, with clear rules for what wins and what gets killed, and turning the winners into playbooks the team can repeat</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>New channels:</strong> finding places where attention is still cheap, from fan pages and communities to platforms nobody on the team is using yet</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organic and paid together:</strong> working with our Growth Manager so organic winners get scaled with paid, and what paid learns feeds back into organic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement:</strong> knowing which number answers which question, for example what saves and shares tell you that views do not, and what each view really costs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling:</strong> building the trackers, scripts and automations you need, with platform data and AI tools as your daily coworkers</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a hands-on organic operator who lives on the platforms, or a creative growth generalist who has made things travel. Either way, you have done it yourself, not through a team or an agency, and you can show the numbers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically, your profile will look like this:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interest:</strong> a strong interest in organic growth, creator marketing and social, ideally with hands-on experience from a startup, brand, app, creator agency or your own channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Breakouts you can show:</strong> you have made things go viral more than once, for a brand, an app or your own channels, and you can explain why it worked and what it cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creator marketing at scale:</strong> you have run creator or UGC programs with many creators at once, negotiated the rates and written briefs that keep the content native; ideally you bring a network of creators, pages and managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform fluency:</strong> you know how TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts distribute content today, what makes a hook, and when a format is burning out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creativity with discipline:</strong> you come up with ideas nobody else would try, and then test them properly, with small budgets, kill rules and numbers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement:</strong> you track reach, engagement and cost per view in your own data, not in screenshots, and you judge every channel by what it brings back</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data and tooling:</strong> you are fast in spreadsheets, ideally comfortable with SQL or Python, and you automate the boring parts with AI tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pace:</strong> you thrive in a fast-paced and performance-oriented environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A big plus:</strong> you are or were a creator yourself, or have run pages with a real following, and you're into media, entertainment, gaming or social</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes this exciting</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own a lever the whole company feels. Every breakout you engineer shows up directly in how fast we can grow, at a fraction of what paid reach would cost. You're not a cog in the machine but the captain of your own ship, rewarded for performance and respected for leadership. Flat hierarchies mean that your voice matters, your ideas get implemented, and your impact is immediate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We pay competitive salaries and make you an owner of the business with equity. We work remotely to give you complete freedom over your life, while meeting regularly around the world for global offsites where we strategize, bond, and push boundaries together.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What the process will look like</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire on a rolling basis. Earliest starting date is always ASAP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Once you begin our process, you can progress from start to offer within a week, depending on how quickly you can move through each stage:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview: 30-minute introductory call, getting to know you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case interview: 90-minute case discussion, present and debate your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder interview: 90-minute interview with our CEO, going deep on all topics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, contract signing and onboarding</p></li></ol><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Note: As we are still in stealth, you will learn more about Melotech as you progress through the stages. By the end of the Founder interview, you will have a full grasp of our business and the details of your role.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/melotech/organic-growth-lead-berlin-122857","tags":["Marketing & Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792226419},{"slug":"founding-head-of-brand-berlin-385658","company_name":"Melotech","title":"Founding Head of Brand","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech is revolutionizing media and entertainment. We create art through technology for humans to enjoy. In just 24 months, our work has been heard, watched and loved for over 4 billion minutes worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by entrepreneur and investor Soheil Mirpour, we are backed by top VCs Cherry Ventures, Speedinvest and GFC, alongside world-class angels from firms such as Spotify, Blackstone and KKR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Melotech's products already reach millions, yet hardly anyone knows the brand. That is where you come in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are our founding brand hire, and you will define what Melotech means to the world from a blank page. There is no brand book, no house style, no established narrative to protect. You decide how we sound, who we are for and why anyone should care, then you make the world take notice. On a typical day, your tasks may include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining our story: one coherent narrative that makes sense of what we are building for fans, press and partners, and keeping it consistent everywhere it shows up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning how the world perceives us across earned media, owned channels, partnerships and the moments we create ourselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with our creatives to ship creative campaigns and stunts that earn attention rather than buy it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opening doors with your own network of press, creators and brands, and turning those relationships into partnerships that would not happen without you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Directing agencies and freelancers on execution while you remain the constant strategic driver</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Laying the reputation groundwork in a category under real public scrutiny, so we lead the hard conversations rather than react to them</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a brand builder who happens to be a communicator, or a communicator who builds brands. You have taken a company from unknown to unmissable before, and you can point at it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically, your profile will look like this:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3 or more years in brand, communications or creative marketing, preferably with real time at an early-stage company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have been part of a zero-to-one brand journey, and you were there early enough to have shaped it rather than inherited it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have shaped a coherent overarching story, not just run communications at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have made things that travelled: campaigns, stunts, formats, moments people talked about</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring a network and you use it. Partnerships you can open yourself are a large part of the value here</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive in a fast-paced and performance-oriented environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A big plus: relationships across media and entertainment, and you're internet-native. You know what's trending, what's breaking, and you're into media, culture or social</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a building role, not a caretaking one: if your best work was producing content at scale or protecting an established brand, this is not the right fit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes this exciting</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get a company that is already working and a brand that does not exist yet. Every decision you make sets the trajectory, and there is nothing to unpick first. You will work directly with our founder, with the freedom to make bold calls and the budget to execute them. You're not a cog in the machine but the captain of your own ship, rewarded for performance and respected for leadership. Flat hierarchies mean that your voice matters, your ideas get implemented, and your impact is immediate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We pay competitive salaries and make you an owner of the business with equity. We work remotely to give you complete freedom over your life, while meeting regularly around the world for global offsites where we strategize, bond, and push boundaries together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What the process will look like</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire on a rolling basis. Earliest starting date is always ASAP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Once you begin our process, you can progress from start to offer within a week, depending on how quickly you can move through each stage:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview: 30-minute introductory call - getting to know you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case interview: 90-minute case discussion - present and debate your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder interview: 90-minute interview with our CEO - going deep on all topics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, contract signing and onboarding</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Note: As we are still in stealth, you will learn more about Melotech as you progress through the stages. By the end of the Founder interview, you will have a full grasp of our business and the details of your role.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/melotech/founding-head-of-brand-berlin-385658","tags":["Marketing & Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792226419},{"slug":"manager-solutions-consultants-dach-munich-132674","company_name":"Notion","title":"Manager, Solutions Consultants, DACH","description":"<h1>Who We Are</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkpYpWfEK5s">think together</a>. We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work is faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about craft, building things that last, and the belief that great work is still fundamentally human. Our goal isn’t to ship the next feature. Each and every team of Notinos is working to set the standard for how humans work together in the AI era. From building a business’s system of record to making and managing AI agents to automating away the busy work, we care deeply about giving our customers more time for their life’s work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the Role:</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Solutions Consultant Manager is the person who makes our GTM motion real on the ground. As an in-region leader directly managing a team of Solutions Consultants, you'll own your team's full commercial output—new logo, expansion, and renewals—and be accountable for both the results and the quality of execution that produces them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't a traditional pipeline-management role. The best SC Managers are coaches first: they know what a great first meeting looks like, can watch a live build and tell a rep exactly what to change, and build the operating rhythm and inspection cadence that makes consistent execution possible across the team. If you're a builder who loves developing people as much as winning deals—and you want to lead a regional team in a go-to-market model that's genuinely new—this is the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be based in Munich, Germany. We work from our offices on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays (our Anchor Days) because we do our best thinking and building together in person. We’re looking for someone who’s excited to work alongside the team during those days. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Achieve:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the commercial performance of your team across new logo ARR, expansion ARR, and UBP outcomes—accountable for both the headline numbers and the quality of execution that drives them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach SCs on the GTM builder motion: what great looks like in a first meeting (workflow diagnosis, current → future architecture), a second meeting (live build in Notion + value narrative), and through the full cycle to adoption hand-off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to and participate in the regional operating cadence: weekly pipeline reviews, deal support sessions, call reviews against the motion quality rubric, and forecast calls with senior leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard, and certify new SCs to the GTM builder motion—driving readiness from ramp through consistent execution, and managing performance with clarity when expectations aren't met</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the regional BDR manager on pipeline strategy, outbound targeting, and qualification standards to ensure the team's book of business is healthy and growing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Outcomes leadership on adoption hand-offs, at-risk account management, and renewal strategy—owning the overall commercial arc for the region while collaborating on the execution that follows close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent your team or region in leadership forums with clear signal on what's working, what needs investment, and where execution is breaking down</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Skills You'll Need to Bring: </h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record as a quota-carrying B2B seller with direct experience in workflow design, live demos, or technical sales—you can coach the builder motion because you've run it yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frontline sales management experience: built an operating cadence, ran performance management, and developed talent from onboarding through consistent overperformance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong coaching orientation: you can watch a demo or deal review and identify specifically what to change—not just whether the outcome was good, but why, and what the rep should do differently next time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial instincts at the team level: able to read pipeline health, identify risk early, and drive urgency across a team without micromanaging individual deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to be an AI expert, but you're curious and willing to adopt AI tools to work smarter and deliver better results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English and German.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Nice to Haves:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling or managing in a consumption or usage-based business where adoption signals matter as much as closed ARR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record building high-performing regional teams from an early stage: hiring to profile, structured onboarding, certification, and performance management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a shared account ownership model—able to navigate the SC/CSA hand-offs and hold the commercial arc across the full customer lifecycle</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is committed to providing highly competitive cash compensation, equity, and benefits. The compensation offered for this role will be based on multiple factors such as location, the role's scope and complexity, and the candidate's experience and expertise, and may vary from the range provided below. The estimated range for total on target earnings (including base salary and on target incentive pay) for this role is €270,000 - €325,000 per year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://notion.notion.site/Notion-Global-Recruiting-Privacy-Policy-fc3eb4e829354a26a2bb6fd5e289b550"><u>Global Recruiting Privacy Policy</u></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dev.notion.so/a3ce416456924276a59de91bca740028?pvs=21"><u>.</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>A Note on AI</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need deep AI expertise for every role, but we do expect every Notino to be intellectually curious, drawn to tinkering and discovery, and excited to use AI as a real collaborator in their work. For some roles, AI fluency is a core requirement — when that’s the case, we'll say so explicitly in the qualifications. People who thrive here don’t treat AI as a novelty. They use it to think better, and make their work easier for others to build on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Equal Opportunity &amp; Accommodations</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire talented people from a wide range of backgrounds. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every bullet, we still encourage you to apply. Notion is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected characteristic. Consistent with applicable law, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Notion provides reasonable accommodations during the application process; if you need one, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Notion considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Notion is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/0ac11447-a862-468b-95a0-40198c971382/5a7e80f3-d875-4693-938a-33455a593625" style="top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0" allowfullscreen scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/notion/manager-solutions-consultants-dach-munich-132674","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich, Germany","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"general-manager-dach-munich-445118","company_name":"Notion","title":"General Manager, DACH","description":"<h1>Who We Are</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkpYpWfEK5s">think together</a>. We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work is faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about craft, building things that last, and the belief that great work is still fundamentally human. Our goal isn’t to ship the next feature. Each and every team of Notinos is working to set the standard for how humans work together in the AI era. From building a business’s system of record to making and managing AI agents to automating away the busy work, we care deeply about giving our customers more time for their life’s work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who We Are:</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits on the EMEA Leadership Team and reports to the General Manager, EMEA.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Achieve:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the GTM strategy, operating rhythm, and growth plan for Germany, with accountability for overall regional revenue outcomes across Sales Assist and Self Serve contribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead as a second-line manager: hire, coach, and develop frontline leaders and IC teams across Business Development, Solutions Consulting, Outcomes Architecture, Forward Deployed Architecture/Engineering, and supporting GTM functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale a country-first GTM motion that brings Notion closer to German customers through local executive engagement, market nuance, and faster field-level decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate the land engine by opening the right front doors, growing professional workspaces, increasing net-new and upgrade opportunities, and connecting self-serve signals to sales-assisted motion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win lighthouse customers and turn them into market momentum by making them wildly successful, telling their story locally, and using those wins to influence peer companies across Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed Notion’s AI-era GTM model across the team, including agent-enabled customer journeys, first-agent workflow activation, AI/agent demo proficiency, and stronger “build with the customer” motions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make agentic transformation central to the German GTM motion: help customers identify high-value workflows, build and deploy Notion Agents, automate cross-functional work, and measure outcomes from AI adoption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner tightly with Solutions Consultants, Outcomes Architects, Forward Deployed Architects/Engineers, Professional Services, and Channel to reduce handoffs and deliver faster, more durable customer value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build “sell with” partner motions in Germany, including partner-sourced pipeline, co-sell plays, enablement, AI/agentic solution packages, and joint account planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish Notion as a visible force in the German ecosystem through executive dinners, field events, startup and community engagement, partner activations, and customer advocacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the voice of German customers back to Product, PMM, Marketing, and EMEA leadership, especially around AI transformation, enterprise requirements, security, compliance, localization, and competitive dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a talent destination in Germany by hiring builder-oriented leaders and ICs, raising the craft bar, and developing the next generation of AI-native GTM talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive operational excellence across forecasting, pipeline quality, territory planning, inspection cadence, performance management, and cross-functional execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Who We're Looking For: </h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strategic and hands-on GTM operator who has scaled enterprise SaaS or AI businesses in Germany and knows how to build a market, not just inherit one. You have led through managers, owned complex revenue outcomes, and created local market momentum through customers, partners, community, and talent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine second-line leadership with builder energy. You can set a crisp country strategy, install the operating system to execute it, and step into the field when needed — whether joining an executive customer conversation, sharpening a pipeline plan, coaching a manager, or helping the team translate a customer problem into an AI-powered, agentic workflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are excited by Notion’s shift to an AI-native, country-first GTM model and believe the best GTM teams will increasingly be builders: BDRs who identify transformation opportunities, Solutions Consultants who build with customers in the room, Outcomes Architects who turn early workflows into durable adoption, and Forward Deployed Architects/Engineers who design the technical systems behind complex agentic workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Skills You'll Need to Bring: </h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12+ years of professional experience, including 5+ years SaaS or AI sales &amp; GTM teams in Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven second-line leadership experience, including hiring, coaching, and developing frontline managers and high-performing IC teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of owning and exceeding revenue targets across new business, expansion, and renewal/churn dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the German enterprise and startup ecosystem, including executive buyer networks, local partner channels, and market-specific buying dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or scaling a regional/country business in a high-growth or ambiguous environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling, implementing, or leading GTM teams around AI, automation, agentic workflows, collaboration, productivity, developer, or data products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong strategic judgment: ability to define a country plan, segment the market, prioritize accounts and plays, and align cross-functional teams around outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational rigor across forecasting, pipeline generation, inspection, performance management, territory planning, and sales process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence with CIO, CTO, CPO, COO, and business transformation buyers, with the ability to shape a compelling AI and agentic workflow narrative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of modern GTM motions across Business Development, Solutions Consulting, Outcomes Architecture, Forward Deployed Architecture/Engineering, Professional Services, Channel, Marketing, RevOps, and Product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builder mentality and deep AI curiosity: comfortable learning, demoing, and coaching teams on agent-first workflows, proof-of-value motions, and customer co-building.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in German and English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Nice to Haves:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience launching or scaling a country-first or regional GTM operating model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with enterprise security, compliance, APIs, webhooks, connectors, data residency, AI governance, and technical evaluation processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience scaling partner, channel, marketplace, or consultant-led GTM motions around AI or workflow transformation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an equal opportunity employer and encourage candidates to apply even if not matching every bullet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is committed to providing highly competitive cash compensation, equity, and benefits. The compensation offered for this role will be based on multiple factors such as location, the role's scope and complexity, and the candidate's experience and expertise, and may vary from the range provided below. The estimated on target earnings (including base salary and on target incentive pay) for this role is €350,000 - 420,000 per year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://notion.notion.site/Notion-Global-Recruiting-Privacy-Policy-fc3eb4e829354a26a2bb6fd5e289b550"><u>Global Recruiting Privacy Policy</u></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dev.notion.so/a3ce416456924276a59de91bca740028?