uctivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP creates value the moment it is connected to our customers' ERP systems. As an Integration Specialist, you onboard our customers on our integrations and ensure connectivity between BLP and their ERP system. You assess and challenge change requests and specify them for our Integration Engineers. Your work directly drives customer go-lives and revenue. Integration Engineers build, Project Managers lead the project, you make the integration work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard customers on our ERP integrations: analyze their IT landscape, engage the right stakeholders, advise on best practices, install and configure our ERP integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess and challenge change requests and turn them into a clear, implementable specification for our Integration Engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customers during self-onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Integration Engineers to continuously improve our integrations and streamline the onboarding experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag major development needs and blockers early, and make clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Project Managers on technical feasibility, effort and sequencing, through first go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in technical consulting, enterprise integration or technical product work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid grasp of ERP landscapes, interfaces and master data, and how data actually moves between them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of at least one ERP system (e.g., Microsoft Dynamics, Oracle, Infor, Abas), both from a functional and integration perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with common integration formats (CSV, XML, JSON) and transports (REST/SOAP APIs, SFTP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of purchase-to-pay (P2P) and order-to-cash (O2C) processes, including the related finance and accounting workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing specifications that engineers can build from without a translation layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable reading production code, with the help of AI tools, to understand integration behavior and answer customer questions.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real impact: successfully connecting a customer's ERP system decides whether a customer goes live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast-growing, global AI company providing the ideal environment to learn and grow fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear handoffs: Integration Engineers build and own the product code, Project Managers own the plan, and you own the implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one month of onboarding at our Zurich headquarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership through our stock option program.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-integration-specialist-munich-14443","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-munich-498986","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Project Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time position based in Munich or Cologne. Following a comprehensive onboarding period at our HQ in central Zurich (minimum one month), you will work from your home location, with regular visits to customers across the DACH region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team collaboration matters a lot to us. You will regularly spend time with the team in person, in Zurich and at our hubs, for team days, all-hands and offsites. These visits are financially supported by blp.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get customers live. Hands on, end to end, and fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>As a Senior Project Manager</strong>, you make large, global blp transformations happen. These programs touch finance, procurement and supply chain at once, run across multiple ERP systems and legal entities, and roll out country by country. Your job is to orchestrate all of it and get the customer live: the first go-live above all, because that is where credibility is won or lost, and then wave after wave with the same discipline. You run the steering committee, you lead a blp team on each engagement, and you do that across several engagements at once.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At both levels, scope is the single biggest lever on whether a project goes live on time. Protecting it is a daily job, not a contract clause. You escalate early and precisely rather than absorbing problems until they become critical.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will not be alone with the technical side. Integrations Engineers handle the connection into the ERP, Technical Project Managers handle the harder solution design, and our Consultants take over the automation work after go-live. On our largest strategic accounts a Client Partner carries the relationship and the commercial number, so your attention goes to delivery quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have done this many times, so you are not inventing the approach each time. A proven onboarding method and a strong toolkit are what let you carry your own customers from early on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Career Path in Project Management</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the path most of our delivery leadership came through, and we hire at every step of it. We place you according to your experience and the size of the programs you have delivered, and we are explicit about what the next step requires.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Manager:</strong> You get customers live end to end, several in parallel: guided onboarding for commercial customers, leading enterprise projects yourself, or a workstream on our largest programs. <em>Typically you bring 2+ years in consulting, implementation or project management.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Senior Project Manager:</strong> You make large, global transformations happen: multiple ERPs, entities and countries, the steering committee, and a blp team on each engagement. <em>Typically you bring 5+ years delivering complex, multi-country programs.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Next steps:</strong> Lead a delivery team, or move into Consulting and from there towards our Client Partner role on strategic accounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moves into Consulting or Customer Success Engineering are open at every level, and many of our people make them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run implementations end to end: kick-off, scope, planning, configuration, testing and go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage several customers in parallel at different stages, and keep every one of them on date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with customers on their processes, and flag early where a process assumption will not hold.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the specialists on your projects: Integrations Engineers, Technical Project Managers and AI Automation Specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own scope actively. Recognize a change request for what it is and handle it deliberately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the project inside its budget, and raise it early when the effort is drifting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand over cleanly at go-live to our Consultants and support organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In addition, as a Senior Project Manager</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery outcome of global programs from kick-off to the last go-live: plan, scope, dependencies and date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the first go-live relentlessly, then run wave planning across ERPs, entities and countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the steering committee and own the decisions that come out of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and execute the recovery plan when a program is off track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the blp team on each engagement and coach the Project Managers working on your programs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Really Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The following key attributes ensure success in this role:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope Discipline – You notice when a project is quietly growing, and you raise it rather than absorbing it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership &amp; Autonomy – You take initiative, move things forward, and deliver end to end without being chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalation Judgment – You escalate early, to the right person, with a proposal rather than a problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Client Confidence – You are comfortable running a meeting with a customer's finance or IT lead in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Four-Language Fluency – Technology, process, data and people. You speak each well enough to spot where a roadblock really sits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured Under Pressure – When a project goes sideways you get sharper and more organized, not louder.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience delivering complex projects: management consulting, enterprise software implementation, or large-scale transformation delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record running multi-country or multi-entity programs with senior client stakeholders, and steering a committee that includes client executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a delivery team rather than only a plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and communication skills. You can translate a business need into something a technical team can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German and English, spoken and written.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points for ERP implementation experience, finance or supply chain processes, or AI-driven SaaS.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership environment – you shape your projects, outcomes, and career path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact at scale – your work powers automation across global enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional exposure – work with engineers, data scientists, and business leaders daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real growth – fast-paced environment, steep learning curve, and structured career progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership – be part of a majority employee-owned company with a best-in-class stock option program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amazing team – become part of a driven and collaborative group of innovators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technology exposure – be at the forefront of AI and enjoy continuous learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visits &amp; offsites – paid visits and stays at our HQ in Zurich, including collaborative team offsites.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to build the future of ERP automation?</strong> Join us and own your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blp.digital/company/careers">https://blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/compani