eadsheets, disconnected tools, and processes that were never built for this moment. <strong>Shiftmove</strong> exists to make this simple.</p><p>We are a profitable B2B SaaS company and the fastest-growing fleet management platform in Europe, born from the merger of Avrios and Vimcar, and now serving tens of thousands of corporate customers across Germany, France, Spain, Switzerland, Poland, and beyond. Most recently, we acquired Optimum and Ocean in France, expanding our footprint and doubling down on one of Europe's largest fleet markets. Our AI-powered platform connects real-time vehicle data with intelligent software so that businesses can procure smarter, control costs, stay compliant, and lead the transition to cleaner mobility, all from one place.<br></p><h3><strong>About the role:</strong></h3><p>We are looking for an experienced <strong>Interim</strong> <strong>Senior BI Analyst</strong> to join us on an initial three-month contract, with the option to extend for a further three months.</p><p>As we integrate two acquired French businesses into our group, we need to bring their data into our standard reporting while transforming how our executive team accesses and uses business intelligence. Our existing Tableau dashboards have evolved over time, and we see an opportunity to make them clearer, more consistent and more actionable.</p><p>Reporting to <strong>our VP of Operations, Data &amp; BI</strong>, you will work closely with the executive team, Head of FP&amp;A, RevOps and Data Engineering. You will take ownership of rebuilding our executive reporting, responding to daily analytical requests and ensuring that acquired-company data is accurately reflected in group-wide reporting.</p><p>This is a hands-on role for someone who combines strong technical BI skills with commercial acumen, sound analytical judgement and the confidence to challenge senior stakeholders when the data tells a different story.<br></p><h3> What You'll Do</h3><ul><li><strong>Rebuild executive reporting:</strong> Audit our existing Tableau dashboards and the underlying business logic. Decide which dashboards to retain, consolidate, redesign or retire, and rebuild the priority dashboards so executives can quickly understand performance and make informed decisions</li><li><strong>Establish consistent metrics:</strong> Document and align metric definitions to ensure that business performance is measured consistently across dashboards, teams and entities</li><li><strong>Own daily ad hoc reporting:</strong> Manage requests through our Jira-based data support queue, prioritising, scoping and delivering analyses on a daily basis. Translate ambiguous requests into clear business questions and identify recurring needs that can be addressed through standard reporting</li><li><strong>Integrate acquisition data:</strong> Partner with Data Engineering as acquired-company data is migrated into Snowflake. Validate and reconcile data against source systems, build and maintain dbt models, and incorporate the data into existing Tableau dashboards so group reporting reflects all entities</li><li><strong>Deliver commercial insights:</strong> Translate executive requirements into meaningful analysis of go-to-market performance, including pipeline, bookings, ARR, retention and churn</li><li><strong>Partner with Finance:</strong> Work closely with the Head of FP&amp;A to reconcile BI reporting with financial figures and establish a consistent view of business performance</li><li><strong>Present findings and challenge assumptions:</strong> Communicate insights directly to the executive team, explain what the data means for the business, and challenge assumptions where the evidence supports a different conclusion</li><li><strong>Enable a smooth handover:</strong> Document dashboards, data models, metric definitions and reporting processes so the permanent BI team can take ownership of the work at the end of the interim period<br></li></ul><h3>What You Need to Succeed</h3>