tegrations that solve it, and turn every win into a reusable pattern the whole company can use.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work as part of Customer Success alongside our Account Owner, and you are the technical partner in the customer's transformation. You will feed what you learn in the field back into our product, and you will have real influence over what we build next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And you will build with our own platform every day. Everyone at Langdock automates their own work with agents and workflows. You will too.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run technical discovery on qualified, high-value use cases: map processes, systems, data flows and constraints with both business and technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build production-grade agents, workflows, Skills, Apps and integrations on Langdock, from first prototype to company-wide rollout.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the implementation of advanced and beta-feature use cases, and of high-profile proofs of concept, together with the Account Owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn individual solutions you built into reusable patterns, templates and on-platform resources, and maintain the bundles repository.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure impact: time saved, costs reduced, tools replaced, quality improved and time to value. Package the results into ROI stories that customers and colleagues can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support our Partners with architecture reviews, high-profile scoping sessions and targeted enablement, so they can deliver independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the technical voice of the customer internally, without losing sight of our principle: Product &gt; Customer Success &gt; Marketing &gt; Sales.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>You Might Be a Fit If…</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 3+ years of experience building production software, data or integration systems, ideally in a customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build with AI, not just talk about it. You have hands-on experience with LLM APIs, agents, tool use, retrieval and workflow automation, and you know how to choose between models and approaches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can talk credibly about data privacy, security, identity and integration architecture with CISOs, IT leads and engineers, because you have solved these problems before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are good at scoping. You know which work is worth doing, you say no to the rest, and you ship what you commit to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You translate business problems into technical designs and technical trade-offs into business terms for executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are commercially aware. You understand that your work drives retention and expansion, and you care about that outcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in German (C1+) and English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a kind person who cares about the people around you.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong> you come from an AI-native company or an early-stage startup. Founder or early-employee experience is a plus, as are public projects such as MCP servers, open-source contributions or AI tooling you have shipped.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The Environment</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work from our office in Berlin, Greifswalder Strasse 212. Everyone works together in person because the hardest problems get solved faster at a whiteboard than in a Slack thread. Days start at 8:30. Lunch and dinner are together. We run, go to the gym, and take care of ourselves. Health is not separate from work here, it is part of how we work well.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The vibe is calm but intense. No one is yelling or panicking. But everyone is working hard on things that matter.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salaries are transparent and tied to levels, not negotiation. All roles include equity. We will figure out the right level together based on your experience and scope. Levels are about the work you own, not your title or years of experience. We narrow down the expected salary range early in the process.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Next steps</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move fast. Most processes complete within two weeks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like your kind of work, we would like to meet you.</p><div><div style="left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4c391c82-4c37-466e-8edf-f3b3b78a1aa2/d48aa50e-3456-44b9-8702-0cc64848c984" style="top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0" allowfullscreen scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><hr><p>Compensation: €90K – €140K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • Base Salary €90K – €140K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/langdock/forward-deployed-engineer-berlin-447106","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792194021},{"slug":"machine-learning-engineer-applied-ai-germany-371827","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Machine Learning Engineer, Applied AI","description":"<h2><strong>About</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are over 5 billion users using basic applications today such email, notes, tasks, calendar and they're not AI-native. Our mission is to build proactive applications for anyone in the world, who are not used to complex prompting. We aim to bring intelligence to conversations, errands, organising and workflows, with minimal to no prompting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first application is an agent-first mobile communication app. We believe building applications that users use daily for communication, coordination and collaboration needs will help integrate AI into their lives. The net effect is to eliminate misinformation, achieve low coordination costs, enable high quality tasks and collaboration at scale with minimal or little prompting.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML systems that power our AI-native applications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on classification, retrieval, ranking, personalization and evaluation, taking ownership from model development to production deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is for engineers who enjoy solving practical ML problems, improving model quality and shipping reliable systems used by real users.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Focus</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML models for classification, ranking, retrieval and personalization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop efficient classifiers and optimize model accuracy, precision, latency and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve search relevance and context retrieval using embeddings, hybrid search and reranking.</p></li><li><p style="min