&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Senior Strategic Account Executive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to&amp;nbsp;sell into high value prospects and customers. This person will play a key role in further growing the business across EMEA with a particular focus on Southern Europe. The candidate will be responsible for managing fast growing customers in the region. Focused mainly on Product cross and up-sell and GP growth, as well as sourcing net new opportunities within a set of accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Servicing the fastest growing customers in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing our revenue and gross profit share of wallet within your key account list.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opening doors to the purchase of Twilio’s products and services - including voice, messaging, email, contact centre, account security software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining the highest levels of customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create pricing proposals, negotiating terms and managing the contract process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selling solutions to a technical and business audience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building trust and mutual respect with technical customers and peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thinking outside of the box and having extraordinary interpersonal and communication skills to make complex contractual, technical, and financial details sound simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balancing challenging priorities and handling multiple projects/deals at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Account Management/Sales experience covering selling and closing complex technical solutions to a large customer base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of working with accounts ranging from large multinational enterprise customers to SMB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success by achieving quota on a consistent basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of Account Management experience and a solid understanding of how to cross sell and upsell solutions within a mature customer base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of financial reporting within a direct customer base - Revenue and Gross Profit tracking, Risk and Opportunity (net new business) cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally, you also have experience selling both to a business and technical audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and understanding of working in the communications market is preferable. Have sold or worked with Messaging, Voice Calling, Email, Account Security Verification. Or have prior experience in a traditional telecommunications environment/business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote, and based in UK, Ireland or Spain&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 25%&amp;nbsp; travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio thinks big. Do you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like to solve problems, take initiative, pitch in when needed, and are always up for trying new things. That&#39;s why we seek out colleagues who embody our values — something we call &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt;Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt;. Additionally, we empower employees to build &lt;a href=&quot;https://twilio.org/support-and-resources/impact-fund&quot;&gt;positive change in their communities&lt;/a&gt; by supporting their volunteering and donation efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, if you&#39;re ready to unleash your full potential, do your best work, and be the best version of yourself, apply now! If this role isn&#39;t what you&#39;re looking for, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/jobs#open-positions&quot;&gt;please consider other open positions.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay alert to recruitment fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about your safety. Scammers sometimes impersonate Twilio recruiters through fake job postings, emails, websites, or messages. Please ensure you are engaging with an official @&lt;a href=&quot;http://twilio.com&quot;&gt;twilio.com&lt;/a&gt; email address. We will never ask for payment, gift cards, cryptocurrency, or banking information during the recruiting process. We do not make job offers without a formal interview process or conduct interviews exclusively through text-based messaging apps.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/strong&gt; We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act. Additionally, Twilio participates in the E-Verify program in certain locations, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/twilio/senior-strategic-account-executive-french-speaker-492990","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792227316},{"slug":"chief-of-staff-uk-london-199214","company_name":"Banyansoftware","title":"Chief of Staff - UK","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialized industries, their employees, and their customers. With a buy-grow-and-hold-for-life approach and a permanent capital base, Banyan acquires and grows companies worldwide, honoring founder legacies and helping portfolio companies modernize through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. Founded in 2016, Banyan operates more than 120 portfolio companies across North and South America, Europe, and APAC, and has appeared on the Inc. 5000 list for six consecutive years. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact opportunity to work directly alongside one of Banyan’s seasoned Operating Leaders, each overseeing a portfolio of software businesses in a buy, hold and grow investment model. As &lt;strong&gt;Chief of Staff&lt;/strong&gt;, you become a trusted right hand to your Operating Leader and a close working partner to the CEOs and functional leaders across their companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is deliberately broad. Rather than a fixed rotation, you will move across multiple operating companies and business problems: shaping a go-to-market plan for one company, improving customer onboarding at another, or standing up the first 100 days of a newly acquired business. You will gain exposure to software M&amp;amp;A, but the core of the job is hands-on value creation and operating work. You own initiatives end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Executive Leadership Program&lt;/strong&gt; (ELP) runs two years. Development is intentional. You will work through a range of experiences spanning go-to-market, M&amp;amp;A, customer, and finance priorities portfolio-wide, plus gain hands-on leadership reps, with regular check-ins and development opportunities to ready you for your next role. High performers move from the ELP program into a CEO or C-suite role within a Banyan operating company, or into a leadership role at Banyan Software HQ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For those who want to learn how great vertical software businesses are built and run, and who want the fastest path available to running one themselves, this is the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Gain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A cohort of high-calibre peers&lt;/strong&gt;. You grow and learn alongside other ELPs at Banyan, building a long-term network of future operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct apprenticeship with senior operators&lt;/strong&gt;. You will work very closely with an Operating Leader and see first-hand how experienced leaders make decisions across different software businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated development support&lt;/strong&gt;. External executive coaching in Year 2, plus mentorship from Operating Leaders with decades of software experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The fastest track we offer to running a business&lt;/strong&gt;. High performers move directly from this program into a C-suite seat inside a Banyan operating company or a leadership role at HQ. It is not guaranteed, performance decides placement, but it is the first place Banyan looks when those seats open and we have a strong track record of placing CEOs through our ELP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real operating reps, not case reps&lt;/strong&gt;. You carry a genuine initiative inside a live business and leadership-level stretch assignments, decisions that show up in a P&amp;amp;L.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Value Creation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CEOs and functional leaders across multiple operating companies to identify priorities and implement the Banyan Operating System, turning strategy into measurable operational improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-impact, cross-functional projects across product, go-to-market, sales, marketing, pricing, and customer success as the right hand to Leader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;M&amp;amp;A and Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain exposure to Banyan’s acquisition process, including value-creation plan framing during diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integration planning and onboarding for newly acquired businesses, helping establish operating rhythms and priorities while respecting what already makes each business work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help execute the value-creation plan once a deal closes, turning the diligence thesis into the specific operating bets a business needs to win in year one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your Operating Leader on critical initiatives, executive decision-making, and cross-company collaboration, frequently influencing outcomes without formal authority or direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the judgment, breadth, and pattern recognition required for future general management by working different business problems across a portfolio of vertical software companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recently graduated from a top MBA program. This cycle is not open to first-year MBA students.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–5 years of pre-MBA experience in an operating role (product, business operations, portfolio operations, or value creation), management consulting, private equity, or investment banking, with a demonstrated record of owning measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and interpersonal judgment, with the ability to synthesize complex information and influence senior stakeholders without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High learning agility and comfort with ambiguity. You get smart quickly in unfamiliar areas, prioritize what matters, and move from analysis to action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego and high ownership. You are ambitious but humble, seek feedback, build trust quickly, and are motivated by the work of operating a business rather than by title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software, SaaS, or another recurring revenue business. Familiarity with vertical software economics is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team. Direct people management is not required; this role initially relies on leadership through influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Equity, Inclusion &amp;amp; Equal Employment Opportunity at Banyan: Banyan affirms that inequality is detrimental to our Global Teams, associates, our Operating Companies, and the communities we serve. As a collective, our goal is to impact lasting change through our actions. Together, we unite for equality and equity. Banyan is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of any protected characteristic, including race, color, genetic information, creed, national origin, religion, sex, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, lawful alien status, ancestry, age, marital status, or protected veteran status and will not discriminate against anyone on the basis of a disability. We support an inclusive workplace where associates excel based on personal merit, qualifications, experience, ability, and job performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Banyan Software does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications submitted via email, LinkedIn, or other direct channels. All candidates must apply through our official Careers site to be considered for employment. Applications submitted outside of our applicant tracking system will not be reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Banyan Software may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to assist in screening and/or assessing applicants during the recruitment process. All hiring decisions are made by our team. Personal information submitted through your application will be collected and used for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable privacy laws. Contact us at any time with questions about our process or to request accommodation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beware of Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have been made aware of individuals fraudulently posing as members of our Talent Acquisition team and extending fake job offers. These scams may involve requests for personal information or payment for equipment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect yourself by following these steps:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify that all communications from our recruiting team come from an ----- email address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remember, employers will &lt;strong&gt;never&lt;/strong&gt; request payment or banking information during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you receive a suspicious message, &lt;strong&gt;do not respond&lt;/strong&gt; — instead, forward it to &lt;a ---------- and/or report it to the platform where you received it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your safety and security are important to us. Thank you for staying vigilant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/banyansoftware/chief-of-staff-uk-london-199214","tags":["Operating Group"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792227316},{"slug":"ai-growth-ops-london-321351","company_name":"Kraken","title":"AI Growth Ops","description":"<h1><strong>Building the Future of Open Finance</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout,  xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Before you apply, we encourage you to explore our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kraken.com/culture"><u>culture page</u></a> to understand what drives us and how we work.</p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2011, Kraken is one of the world's longest-standing crypto platforms, trusted by over 10 million individuals and institutions across the globe. It offers spot trading, margin, futures, staking, and OTC services, with products built for both individual investors and institutional clients.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth at Kraken is being rebuilt around an AI-native platform. Instead of people manually building audiences, writing copy, adjusting budgets, and scheduling sends, agents find opportunities, make decisions, and execute across paid, organic, and lifecycle channels. They learn from every result and keep going.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">People still run the system. Operators use a central hub to set the rules the agents follow, review and approve what they produce, and handle exceptions when something doesn’t fit. The platform also has to work across many markets and languages, and it operates in a regulated industry, so there are compliance checks and approval steps built in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team is a small, cross-functional group of growth, product, and engineering people who build this platform and run it day to day. We ship often, learn fast, and raise the quality bar with every release. You will work most closely with the engineers building the platform, the product team defining how operators use it, and the operators who rely on it every day. QA and operations is how the whole team knows the platform can be trusted.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own day-to-day operations and QA for our internal growth platform. You test it, catch problems before our customers do, keep approvals and exception queues moving, and report on how it’s performing. You will work closely with product, engineering and operators to make sure the platform works and keeps working.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on, detail-focused role. You will spend your days in the product, testing what’s new, checking what should already work, and writing up what you find so it gets fixed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test the platform regularly. Cover new releases, rule changes, and edge cases, and run regression checks to make sure existing features still work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find bugs and document them clearly, with steps to reproduce, severity, and impact. Follow them through until engineering fixes them and you’ve verified the fix.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor platform performance and agent activity, flag anything that looks wrong, and escalate it to the right person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work the approval queues daily. Keep items moving and make sure nothing is left unreviewed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check agent output against defined checklists and standards, and escalate anything unclear or risky.Note where flows are confusing or inconsistent, and flag them to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and maintain documentation: test plans, QA checklists, runbooks, and release notes.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in QA, testing, operations, support, or analytics, ideally on a software product or complex system</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail. You notice what others miss and double-check your work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured approach to testing. You can create and follow a test plan, and think about what could break.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written communication. Your bug reports and documentation should be easy for anyone to follow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with data. You can read a dashboard and tell when a number looks off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fast learner. You pick up new tools and systems quickly and ask thoughtful questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI-native habits. You use AI tools in your own work every day, and you’re curious about where they get things wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prompt engineering curiosity, you don't need to be an engineer, but you are willing to learn how to communicate with AI systems precisely and improve their outputs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliability. You keep to a routine, keep your queues clear, and tell people early when something is stuck.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience testing software products or AI and LLM-based tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Jira, Mixpanel, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to marketing, CRM, or lifecycle messaging workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in fintech or crypto</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless a specific application deadline is stated in the job posting, applications are accepted on an ongoing basis.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Please note, applicants are permitted to redact or remove information on their resume that identifies age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We consider qualified applicants with criminal histories for employment on our team, assessing candidates in a manner consistent with the requirements of the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our commitment</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward is powered by people from around the world and we celebrate the diverse talents, backgrounds, contributions, and unique perspectives that everyone brings to the table. We hire based on merit, seeking out people with the right abilities, knowledge, and skills for the job. We encourage you to apply for roles where you don't fully meet the listed requirements, especially if you're passionate or knowledgeable about crypto.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We may ask candidates to complete job-related skills or work-style assessments as part of our hiring process. These assessments evaluate competencies relevant to the role and are applied consistently across candidates for similar positions. Results are considered alongside experience and interviews, and are not the sole basis for any employment decision.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an equal opportunity employer, we don't tolerate discrimination or harassment of any kind, whether based on race, ethnicity, age, gender identity, citizenship, religion, sexual orientation, disability, pregnancy, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay connected</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://twitter.com/krakenfx"><u>Follow us on Twitter</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://blog.kraken.com/#:~:text=Enter%20your%20email%20address"><u>Learn on the Kraken Blog</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/kraken-exchange/"><u>Connect on LinkedIn</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kraken.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice"><u>Candidate Privacy Notice</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kraken/ai-growth-ops-london-321351","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792226417},{"slug":"associate-ii-product-operations-london-262159","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Associate II, Product Operations","description":"<h1><strong>Building the Future of Open Finance</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout,  xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Before you apply, we encourage you to explore our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kraken.com/culture"><u>culture page</u></a> to understand what drives us and how we work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2011, Kraken is one of the world's longest-standing crypto platforms, trusted by over 10 million individuals and institutions across the globe. It offers spot trading, margin, futures, staking, and OTC services, with products built for both individual investors and institutional clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Krak is Kraken's consumer banking and payments product — a fast-moving team building the card, payments, and financial features that bring crypto to everyday life. The Krak Product Operations team sits at the heart of this, making sure the business can move quickly without getting blindsided by compliance, risk, vendor, or operational dependencies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is one of two roles in Krak’s Product Ops function, reporting to the Manager, Product Ops - Krak. You'll bring leadership to the day-to-day, working directly with compliance, legal, fraud, client engagement (CE), and external vendors to make sure new features land safely and successfully.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Ops at Krak is a co-ordination and intelligence function. Your job is to make sure that the cross-functional dependencies that could slow or derail delivery are surfaced early, actively managed, and resolved. You'll also help the team make better product decisions by curating the right operational data and bringing market and vendor intelligence into the room.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work across four areas: compliance and risk co-ordination, third party vendor management, responding to management information (MI) and feature performance, and strategic market intelligence. Your job is to make sure the right conversations happen at the right time, and that nothing falls through the cracks on the way to launch.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Compliance &amp; risk co-ordination</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain live, product-specific trackers of open compliance and legal items, including DRIs, status, and upcoming milestones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Triage new features against regulatory requirements ahead of development; ensure sign-off is built into delivery milestones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with fraud leads to ensure fraud controls and risk/velocity rules are factored into feature design (card, third party payments, and others)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure fraud and CE teams are operationally positioned - with the right tooling, admin access, battlecards, and support articles - ahead of new product and feature launches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support incident response for product-related issues and ensure post-incident reviews feed into product changes</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Third party vendor management</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain product-specific vendor trackers covering status, open actions, key contacts, and upcoming milestones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the cadence for performance reviews with key vendors and track actions to closure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a working view 