&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, Graphcore offers flexible working, a generous annual leave policy, private medical insurance and health cash plan, a dental plan, pension (matched up to 5%), life assurance and income protection. We have a generous parental leave policy and an employee assistance programme (which includes health, mental wellbeing, and bereavement support). We offer a range of healthy food and snacks at our central Bristol office and have our own barista bar! We welcome people of different backgrounds and experiences; we’re committed to building an inclusive work environment that makes Graphcore a great home for everyone. We offer an equal opportunity process and understand that there are visible and invisible differences in all of us. We can provide a flexible approach to interview and encourage you to chat to us if you require any reasonable adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Applicants for this position must hold the right to work in the UK. Unfortunately at this time, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support for visa applications&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/graphcore/senior-software-engineer-in-build-engineering-london-94528","tags":["Software Ops"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792216515},{"slug":"senior-rfp-bid-manager-emea-aachen-111068","company_name":"Keyfactorinc","title":"Senior RFP & Bid Manager, EMEA","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Keyfactor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our mission is to securely connect the world: humans, machines, and AI. Keyfactor is the leader in trust infrastructure for AI and machines, helping the world&#39;s largest enterprises and government agencies take control of the cryptographic identities that safeguard every digital interaction. Behind the platform is a global team of people who care deeply about the work and each other. We move fast, think big, and show up for one another every day. If you&#39;re looking for work that matters and a team that brings out your best, we hope you&#39;ll trust your future with Keyfactor!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title&lt;/strong&gt;: Senior RFP &amp;amp; Bid Manager, EMEA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: Stockholm, Sweden; Aachen, Germany; Barcelona or Madrid, Spain; United Kingdom&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Senior&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Function&lt;/strong&gt;: Revenue Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type&lt;/strong&gt;: Full-Time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry&lt;/strong&gt;: Computer and Network Security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;About the position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior RFP &amp;amp; Bid Manager, EMEA is responsible for establishing, managing, and continuously improving the RFP, RFI, and tender response management framework across Keyfactor&#39;s EMEA sales organization. Operating as a specialized individual contributor, the role owns the operational processes, governance standards, tools, and knowledge management practices required to support effective and consistent bid responses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position coordinates the end-to-end RFP response process, working closely with Sales, Solutions Engineering, and other relevant departments to obtain required inputs, manage timelines and dependencies, and facilitate accurate, complete, and timely submissions. The role applies specialized knowledge of bid management practices and procurement procedures to identify operational risks, recommend appropriate response approaches, and drive improvements in process effectiveness and efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of a newly established function, the role develops scalable operating practices and documentation to support the continued development of RFP management capabilities within EMEA and potential future adoption in other regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position can be based out of our offices in following locations and we have a hybrid work model: Stockholm (Sweden), Barcelona or Madrid (Spain), Aachen, Germany or United Kingdom.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Header 1 [H1]&quot; data-ccp-parastyle-defn=&quot;{&amp;quot;ObjectId&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;78ec3665-3fe7-4df3-9ceb-b5e5c3a6b84d|202&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;ClassId&amp;quot;:1073872969,&amp;quot;Properties&amp;quot;:[469777841,&amp;quot;Degular Medium&amp;quot;,469777844,&amp;quot;Degular Medium&amp;quot;,469769226,&amp;quot;Degular Medium&amp;quot;,335551500,&amp;quot;16736607&amp;quot;,268442635,&amp;quot;44&amp;quot;,335559740,&amp;quot;240&amp;quot;,201341983,&amp;quot;0&amp;quot;,335559739,&amp;quot;360&amp;quot;,201342446,&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;,201342447,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;,201342448,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;,201342449,&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;,469777842,&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,469777843,&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,201341986,&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;,335559738,&amp;quot;0&amp;quot;,335559682,&amp;quot;0&amp;quot;,335560102,&amp;quot;0&amp;quot;,134245418,&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;,134245529,&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;,469775450,&amp;quot;Header 1 [H1]&amp;quot;,201340122,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;,134234082,&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;,134233614,&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;,469778129,&amp;quot;Header1H1&amp;quot;,335572020,&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;,335559685,&amp;quot;432&amp;quot;,335559991,&amp;quot;432&amp;quot;,469775498,&amp;quot;Normal&amp;quot;,469778324,&amp;quot;heading 1&amp;quot;]}&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245529&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:432,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:432}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;page-1&quot; class=&quot;_kqswh2mm _bfhku67f _18u01wug _2hwx1wug&quot; data-testid=&quot;page-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and continuously improve the EMEA RFP and bid management operating framework&lt;/strong&gt;, establishing standardized intake procedures, response workflows, submission controls, and governance practices to ensure consistent and effective execution across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate the end-to-end execution of complex RFP, RFI, and tender responses&lt;/strong&gt;, working closely with Sales, Solutions Engineering, Legal, Compliance, and other relevant functions to obtain required inputs, manage timelines and dependencies, and ensure timely, accurate, and complete submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and continuously improve bid management methodologies and standards&lt;/strong&gt;, identifying operational inefficiencies, evaluating improvement opportunities, and implementing solutions to enhance response quality, turnaround time, and cross-functional effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply specialized knowledge of public and private tender procedures&lt;/strong&gt;, assessing procedural requirements, identifying submission risks, and providing guidance to internal stakeholders on appropriate response processes while escalating matters requiring legal, compliance, or commercial decisions to the relevant functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish and govern a centralized RFP content and knowledge management framework&lt;/strong&gt;, including the administration of Loopio and approved supporting tools, ensuring content accuracy, consistency, currency, and appropriate validation by relevant subject-matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitate effective cross-functional collaboration throughout the bid response process&lt;/strong&gt;, coordinating contributions from Sales, Solutions Engineering, Product Management, Legal, Compliance, Finance, and Professional Services, and ensuring that dependencies, responsibilities, and escalation requirements are clearly communicated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise independent professional judgment in managing RFP response activities&lt;/strong&gt;, determining when approved content can be used, identifying requirements for additional specialist input, and escalating complex or sensitive matters to the appropriate accountable stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate the review and validation of technical, security, service-related, and contractual information included in bid responses&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring that product capabilities, roadmap statements, security representations, implementation commitments, and service deliverables are reviewed and approved by the relevant authorized functions prior to submission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as the primary operational point of contact for customer procurement representatives and external bid management partners&lt;/strong&gt;, coordinating procedural clarifications, submission requirements, joint-bid activities, and response logistics while involving Sales and other relevant stakeholders in substantive customer discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain RFP management performance reporting&lt;/strong&gt;, monitoring submission volumes, turnaround times, response quality, content effectiveness, and relevant bid outcomes, analyzing operational trends, and recommending process improvements to Revenue Operations and Sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide specialized functional guidance to internal stakeholders on bid management practices&lt;/strong&gt;, supporting the consistent application of established workflows, tender procedures, governance standards, and RFP management tools across the EMEA sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain scalable bid management documentation and implementation playbooks&lt;/strong&gt;, establishing repeatable methodologies and operating practices that support the ongoing development of the EMEA function and potential future adoption in other regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Minimum Qualifications, Education, and Skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:264}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Management, Communications, or a related field, or equivalent relevant professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Knowledge &amp;amp; Job Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in RFP management, proposal management, bid management, or a closely related function, preferably within B2B software or technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience coordinating complex RFPs, RFIs, and tenders involving multiple internal functions and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience establishing, improving, or governing structured bid response processes, including standardized workflows, content management practices, and operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of public and private procurement processes, including open, restricted, negotiated, and competitive dialogue procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying procedural and operational risks and coordinating their resolution with relevant internal subject-matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with RFP management platforms and content repositories; experience with Loopio is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently prioritize RFP activities, manage competing deadlines, and determine when additional specialist input or escalation is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Sales, technical specialists, Legal, Compliance, and Professional Services in complex bid response environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with B2B software environments; experience in cybersecurity, PKI, or information security is advantageous but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APMP certification or a comparable professional qualification is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Skill&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong bid and proposal project management skills, including planning, prioritization, stakeholder coordination, and deadline management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated process design, documentation, governance, and continuous improvement skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess procedural requirements, identify operational risks, and recommend appropriate solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication and content review skills, ensuring accuracy, clarity, and consistency in customer-facing submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional stakeholder management and influencing skills, with the ability to coordinate contributors without direct reporting authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in RFP management tools, structured content repositories, and business productivity applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze operational performance data and translate findings into practical process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple concurrent priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to work effectively across diverse teams and cultures within EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently within broadly defined procedures, policies, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to apply specialized knowledge and sound professional judgment to complex bid management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish and continuously improve operational processes in a developing functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coordinate multiple stakeholders and manage dependencies while maintaining effective working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify potential operational, procedural, and submission risks and determine appropriate escalation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence stakeholders through specialized expertise, collaboration, and effective communication rather than formal organizational authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain accuracy, consistency, and attention to detail under competing deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt working methods and priorities to changing business requirements across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distinguish operational decisions within the role&#39;s authority from matters requiring formal technical, legal, compliance, or commercial approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Travel Requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Up to 15% travel time required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt; color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-NA1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary will be commensurate with experience. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture, Career Opportunities and Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build teams that continually strive to get better than the day before. You will be challenged daily and given opportunities to grow personally and professionally. We balance autonomy and structure to create an entrepreneurial environment to spur creativity and new ideas. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are just some of the initiatives that make our culture special:  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Second Fridays (a company-wide day off on the second Friday of every month minus November and December due to the Holiday schedule). Please note that this benefit is subject to change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefit coverage globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave is available to new parents. Structure varies based on regional/government requirements. In regions where government-paid leave doesn’t exist, like in the U.S., the company offers generous paid parental leave, along with comprehensive adoption and fertility support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive time off globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicated employee-focused ambassadors via Key Contributors &amp;amp; Culture Committees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DIVERSE Commitment, a call to action for a more inclusive and diverse future in business, society, and technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Keyfactor Alliance Program to support DEIB efforts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing resources, wellness allowance, mindfulness app free membership, Wellness Wednesdays.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Volunteer Day, company non-profit matching, and 3 volunteer days off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Talent development and Cross Functional meetings to support professional development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular All Hands meetings – followed by group gatherings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Core Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our core values are extremely important to how we run our business and what we look for in every team member:  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is paramount.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We deliver security software and solutions where trust and openness are of the highest importance for our customers. We are honest and a trusted partner in every aspect of business.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; are core.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strategize, operate, and execute through a customer-centric view. We prioritize the security interests of our customers, and we act as if their data were our own.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; never stops, it only accelerates.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The speed of change is accelerating. We are committed, through investment and focus, to stay ahead of the innovation curve.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We deliver with &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;agility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We thrive in high-paced and continually changing environments. We navigate through newly added variables, adjust accordingly, while driving towards our strategic goals.  &lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;United by &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;respect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Respect for all is what unites us. We promote diversity, inclusivity, equity, and acting with empathy and openness, both in our business and in our communities.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; make “it” happen.&lt;/strong&gt;  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vision and goals are not individually achievable – they require teamwork. We pride ourselves in operating as a cohesive team, creating promoters and partners, and winning as one.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keyfactor is a proud equal opportunity employer including but not limited to veterans and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REASONABLE ACCOMMODATION: &lt;/strong&gt;Applicants with disabilities may contact a member of Keyfactor’s People team via ----- and/or telephone at 1.216.785.2990 to request and arrange for accommodations at any time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.keyfactor.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Keyfactor Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/keyfactorinc/senior-rfp-bid-manager-emea-aachen-111068","tags":["Business Transformation"],"job_types":[],"location":"Aachen","created_at":1792216514},{"slug":"affiliate-and-influencer-marketer-old-street-54297","company_name":"Granola","title":"Affiliate and Influencer Marketer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.granola.ai/"><u>Granola</u></a> is the AI notepad for people in back-to-back meetings. We're growing fast and looking for a hands-on affiliate / influencer / creator marketer to help us scale our partnership programmes across evergreen and launch campaigns. This is an individual contributor role.<br /></p><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an affiliate and influencer marketer to join our team at Granola. We work with hundreds of creators and publishers to support acquiring new users through partnerships (sponsorships, affiliation and hybrid models).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll sit at the intersection of branding and growth, making sure we’re proud of the online narratives around Granola and checking the performance of our influencer marketing efforts at a channel and partner level.<br /></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own a creator portfolio</strong> : Be responsible for growing and looking after a large portfolio of key accounts (sponsored, affiliates or hybrid) and regularly keeping in touch with them to increase Granola’s presence on their different channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Newsletter sponsorships </strong>: You'll own this channel end to end, from partner onboarding and booking through live-date tracking, invoicing, and performance reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influencer partnerships :</strong> Sourcing and onboarding great creators for authentic collaborations. Instead of an ad placement, you’ll do demos of granola, find ideas and creative briefs for the influencers that would bring new user acquisitions too</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>YouTube collaborations </strong>: Running campaigns with youtube creators to meet internal priorities through integrations, dedicated videos and editorial projects.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Example projects you might work on</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Newsletter creatives : </strong>draft launch announcements and evergreen copy, and work with our design and copywriting team to get assets for our ads placements. Review editorial pieces for accuracy and brand safety.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AEO portfolio.</strong> Increase the amount of citations on LLM through YouTube partnerships and listicle sponsorships, measuring the impact on citations from your work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account management :</strong> being the point of contact for a portfolio of affiliates / creators with large audiences, building win-win deals and generating authentic content.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your background looks something like…</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3 years in <strong>influencer / affiliate marketing</strong>, brand-side or agency side. You’ve worked on significant creator collaborations that had tangible business impact (we’ll ask for example of campaigns you’ve run or a portfolio)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of <strong>managing a large portfolio of accounts</strong> and co-building the systems to support working with hundreds of vendors and deals at once, without sacrificing the quality of deliverables</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working at a startup or scale up, preferably in tech, AI or B2B SaaS space. You understand the future of work and Granola’s ICP (enterprise and self-serve)</p></li></ul><h2><strong>As a person, you…</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have high-agency and business acumen. You’re able to autonomously allocate budget, negotiate with creators, unstuck collaborations including at-risk accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are AI-native but know when to use it and when it is an overkill</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are extremely good at prioritizing - picking what will really move the needles with goals and saying no to what is just busy work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have deep interest, curiosity and understanding around the creator economy and brand partnerships. You know that the playbooks get constantly re-written and you proactively keep up with the industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are chronically online and already know partners that would be a great fit for Granola. Bonus if you have existing relationships with creators, publishers and key opinion leaders that would be a great fit for Granola.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are creative and can select creators who have a tasteful editorial line and content style. You’d be able to scout the partners we’d be proud to collaborate with not only through data but also by instincts. Your experience helps you tell who can build trust and influence.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About the opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the opportunity to come shape the narrative of Granola with creators while generating measurable growth, on the branding and user acquisition side, and create business impact at one of the fastest growing AI company in London.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work primarily together in London (office-first). You can find more about the team, how we work and our benefits on our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.granola.ai/jobs"> <u>careers page</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like work you’d love doing, we’d like to hear from you—even if your experience doesn’t match every point above.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our compensation philosophy is to hire the best people in the market and pay them accordingly with salary, variable, and equity.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/granola/affiliate-and-influencer-marketer-old-street-54297","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792215633},{"slug":"sales-executive-london-240644","company_name":"Zego","title":"Sales Executive","description":"<h2><strong>About Zego 🚀</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Zego, we're on a mission to do the good thing, not the insurance thing.<br /><br />Insurance hasn't changed much in over a century. The way we live, work and travel has. We're building the real-time, AI-driven infrastructure that powers innovative insurance, so good drivers get cover that works the way they actually drive.<br /><br /><strong>We're not just updating insurance; We're leading the AI evolution in insurance </strong>🤖</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For us, AI isn't a line on a roadmap or a buzzword on a slide. It's our operating reality, and it's how we build products that back drivers instead of the old insurance playbook.<br /><br />We don't do things slowly, and we don't do bureaucracy. We back high-performance builders who want ownership, early responsibility and the chance to do the most career-defining work of their lives. You'll get the space to try things, the tools to move fast, and the room to see your ideas reach millions of drivers.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do not take our word for it. Read what Zegons say about us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Zego-Insurance-EI_IE1851459.11,25.htm"><u>Glassdoor</u></a>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to build the future of insurance,<strong> we're hiring.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work through the new and existing business leads by making outbound calls to prospective customers, helping them through the sales process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll deal with incoming sales calls, mid-term adjustments, renewals and returning customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will assess customers insurance needs and advice on appropriate Zego insurance products, whilst always following compliance guidelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will ensure customer satisfaction and provide professional customer support over phone, live chat and email.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will maintain a positive, empathetic and professional attitude towards customers at all times and build productive trust relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will respond promptly to customer inquiries whilst making sure all communication is documented and logged in our internal system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will follow GDPR guidelines and processes in all communication with customers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will need to be successful</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have proven skills working within a high performing target-driven customer call centre- sales and service environment, ideally in a call centre setting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked in a high target environment, high revenue, daily call targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are obsessive about customer experience and act as an advocate for our customer’s needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're able to listen to customers and be able to give advice and support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an ability to multitask, set priorities and manage time effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have a good understanding of GDPR rules and regulations and be able to use multiple systems at the same time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, you will have experience in insurance or an FCA regulated business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Zego ways of working 🏡</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teams work better with time to collaborate and space to get things done. We call it Zego Hybrid: some of us are in our office (central London or Halifax) weekly, others monthly or quarterly. It's about finding the balance between face time and focus that produces great work and a healthy life around it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also make a point of getting everyone in the same room. Teams come together every quarter, and once a year the whole company does, properly. It's a serious investment and consistently one of the best parts of the year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QKOYDx6AMxQ"><u>Here is what the last one looked like</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits 🎁</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Market-competitive salary, benchmarked against your function and reviewed every year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏆 Annual performance bonus, linked to company performance and your contribution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Share options, a real stake in the company and a share in the future you build</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private medical insurance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏖️ Pension, generous holiday, and £1,000 a year to spend on getting to the office or learning something new.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Cutting-edge systems and tools, so you always have what you need to drive your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? We want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zego, leading the AI evolution in insurance.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunities 🌈</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We're an equal opportunity employer and we value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability status.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zego/sales-executive-london-240644","tags":["Customer Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792215633},{"slug":"policy-manager-london-96915","company_name":"Plaid","title":"Policy Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that the way people interact with their finances will drastically improve in the next few years. We’re dedicated to empowering this transformation by building the tools and experiences that thousands of developers use to create their own products. Plaid powers the tools millions of people rely on to live a healthier financial life. We work with thousands of companies like Venmo, SoFi, several of the Fortune 500, and many of the largest banks to make it easy for people to connect their financial accounts to the apps and services they want to use. Plaid’s network covers 12,000 financial institutions across the US, Canada, UK and Europe. Founded in 2013, the company is headquartered in San Francisco with offices in New York, Seattle, Washington D.C., Raleigh, London, and Amsterdam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Plaid’s Public Policy Manager for the UK and EU, you’ll lead our policy work across both regions, partnering closely with our Head of Policy and Head of Europe Legal and Compliance. You’ll advocate for a secure, consumer-friendly financial ecosystem where people can use their financial data to access the products and services they need. The work spans some of the most important and fast-moving issues in financial services, from cybersecurity and privacy to data use and competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a resourceful, strategic thinker who reads political and regulatory dynamics well and finds a way forward. You’ll translate technical and business concepts into clear, actionable policy positions that help grow Plaid’s business and benefit our customers and the consumers they serve. If you’re high-agency, creative in your approach, and known for exceptional follow-through, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and own relationships with regulators, government officials, and legislators across the UK and EU, as well as consumer groups, trade associations, financial institutions, and other key stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Plaid in industry working groups and policy forums on open banking, open finance, smart data, payments, security, and privacy, making Plaid’s case and spotting opportunities to shape the conversation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead research and analysis that shapes Plaid’s positions on key issues and informs our regulatory engagement and advocacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the planning and execution of Plaid’s UK and EU policy agenda, coordinating projects with internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with teams across Legal, Compliance, Communications, Marketing, Product, Engineering, and Sales on shared initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay ahead of emerging policy trends in the UK and EU, flagging risks and opportunities for Plaid’s business and recommending strategies for engagement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of experience in UK or EU financial services policy, for example at a regulator such as the Financial Conduct Authority (FCA), in government (such as HM Treasury), in Parliament, at a financial services trade association, or in-house.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong existing relationships with policymakers, regulators, financial institutions, trade associations, think tanks, and consumer groups in the UK or EU.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of advocacy and policy influence within financial services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build consensus among diverse stakeholders, including those across the political spectrum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A resourceful, adaptable, and collaborative approach, with a willingness to roll up your sleeves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about product, technology, and AI.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-Haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Policy experience across both the UK and EU.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working on open banking, open finance, payments, or data-sharing policy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in London.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission at Plaid is to unlock financial freedom for everyone. To support that mission, we seek to build a diverse team of driven individuals who care deeply about making the financial ecosystem more equitable. We recognize that strong qualifications can come from both prior work experiences and lived experiences. We encourage you to apply to a role even if your experience doesn't fully match the job description. We are always looking for team members that will bring something unique to Plaid!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plaid is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and values diversity at our company. We do not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion or religious belief, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, sexual stereotypes, age, military or veteran status, disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws. Plaid is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities in our recruiting process. If you need any assistance with your application or interviews due to a disability, please let us know at ----- style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please review our Candidate Privacy Notice <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://plaid.com/legal/#candidate-privacy-notice"><u>here</u></a>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional compensation in the form(s) of equity and/or commission are dependent on the position offered. Plaid provides a comprehensive benefit plan, including medical, dental, vision, and 401(k). Pay is based on factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and skillset, and location. Pay and benefits are subject to change at any time, consistent with the terms of any applicable compensation or benefit plans.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/plaid/policy-manager-london-96915","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"GBR - LON Metro","created_at":1792215633},{"slug":"developer-portal-community-manager-london-83158","company_name":"Flipper","title":"Developer Portal & Community Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are the creators of<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://flipperzero.one/"> <strong><u>Flipper Zero</u></strong></a> — a portable device for tech enthusiasts and engineers. It’s a gadget with an awesome community that brings together millions of people around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a new product —<strong> Flipper One</strong>. It’s a full-featured ARM-based computer running Linux in a compact form factor, powered by the Rockchip RK3576 SoC.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve decided to make the entire development process completely open and public. That’s why we’re looking for a <strong>Developer Portal &amp; Community Manager</strong> to own and manage the entire Flipper One Developer Portal: maintaining the wiki, collecting tasks from all development teams, managing all GitHub projects and repositories, and proactively communicating with the community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is perfect for you if you want to be close to the product, see firsthand how it’s built, and help turn that process into a clear and valuable entry point for the community. This is not a “content manager” role — you’ll need to fully understand the development process, track all ongoing tasks, and connect the team with the community to make things happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is the Developer Portal?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Developer Portal is a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.flipper.net/one"><u>public wiki</u></a> + a set of GitHub projects built around Flipper One. It documents how the project works as a whole, explains the architecture of its major subsystems, and provides contribution guides for the community — showing how people can contribute to each sub-project.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Anyone reading the Developer Portal wiki should come away with a complete understanding of the project structure, each feature, and what exactly we are building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clearly, concisely, and without fluff, and can show examples of your work: guides, instructions, READMEs, how-tos, or similar materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic understanding of hardware, software, and development workflows (Git, commits, branches, pull requests)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to explain complex technical topics in simple language and visualize them with flowchart sketches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong verbal communication skills; you know how to listen, ask precise questions, and quickly extract the key points from chaotic discussions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep communication with the community productive — without toxicity, unnecessary softness, or bureaucracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable collaborating closely with engineers and navigating technical contexts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discern useful feedback and constructive disagreement from noise and spam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Value structure, logic, clarity, and information quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuinely interested in developer-facing products, hardware, documentation, open communities, and the build-in-public approach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proficiency in Russian and English</strong> for communication with other departments in the company and the external community</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in DevRel, technical writing, community operations, or an editorial role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with documentation, wikis, knowledge bases, or developer portals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of the culture of technical communities, open-source, and hardware projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work across topics at the intersection of interfaces, electronics, product architecture, and internal development</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilites:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and develop the Flipper One Developer Portal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn the team’s internal context into clear public documentation, notes, updates, and explanations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join team calls to understand what’s actually happening in the project and maintain a complete picture of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate technical discussions into clear, human language without losing meaning or accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moderate community comments, pull requests, and contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filter out spam, reduce noise, and keep discussions productive</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help users understand how the portal works and how to provide useful feedback</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collect signals from the community and bring them back to the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure the portal stays structured, up to date, and genuinely useful</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Fully remote from anywhere in the world</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be provided with all the necessary equipment for a comfortable working environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits such as VHI, corporate sports, foreign language courses, and therapy sessions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A five-day workweek with a flexible start of the working day</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/flipper/developer-portal-community-manager-london-83158","tags":["Content"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1792215632},{"slug":"quality-manager-manufacturing-operations-bristol-the-crescent-112966","company_name":"Fractile","title":"Quality Manager- Manufacturing Operations","description":"<h1><strong>About Fractile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile was founded in 2022 on the bet that, eventually, the world’s most capable AI systems would be limited in their impact by the time taken to produce useful outputs. We bet everything on the logical conclusion: that the only way to truly unlock this latent value, to make speed viable at scale, was to radically re-invent the hardware that we run our frontier AI models on. Ever since, we have been building chips and systems that tackle this problem: how to efficiently generate output at thousands of tokens per second, while handling the complexity and capacity challenges of operating large models at very long contexts.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The workloads that push to the limits of the current frontier are already transformational; it is the technical and economic limits on inference speed that are constraining progress. The defining work of the 21st century will be marked by the engine of inference delivering immense and diffuse chains of intellectual inquiry, in drug discovery, in software engineering, in materials discovery, in any field where progress is driven by deep reasoning and intelligence to resolve complex problems. </p><h2><strong>About Fractile</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile was founded in 2022 on the bet that, eventually, the world’s most capable AI systems would be limited in their impact by the time taken to produce useful outputs. We bet everything on the logical conclusion: that the only way to truly unlock this latent value, to make speed viable at scale, was to radically re-invent the hardware that we run our frontier AI models on. Ever since, we have been building chips and systems that tackle this problem: how to efficiently generate output at thousands of tokens per second, while handling the complexity and capacity challenges of operating large models at very long contexts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The workloads that push to the limits of the current frontier are already transformational; it is the technical and economic limits on inference speed that are constraining progress. The defining work of the 21st century will be marked by the engine of inference delivering immense and diffuse chains of intellectual inquiry, in drug discovery, in software engineering, in materials discovery, in any field where progress is driven by deep reasoning and intelligence to resolve complex problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in the UK you will be a key member of the Manufacturing Operations team where you will drive the development of our business management systems as well as our product, supplier, software and customer quality initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be comfortable with assessing processes and technologies to identify quality gaps and provide robust but pragmatic solutions to drive all aspects of the business in achieving the highest levels of quality and resilience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and deliver the company quality strategy, policy and objectives, aligned to the product roadmap and growth plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, lead and develop a quality team covering supplier, product, reliability, software and systems quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and report quality performance to the executive team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish appropriate document control, change control, CAPA, internal audit, training and records processes that scale with a fast-growing fabless company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with PMO to embed quality gates into the new product introduction (NPI) and product lifecycle process, from concept through end of life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own quality across the supply chain: wafer foundry, assembly and packaging, wafer and final test, PCB/PCBA and system-level contract manufacturers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead supplier selection, qualification, audits and ongoing performance management, including scorecards and quarterly business reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineering leaders to define software quality standards across drivers, firmware, compilers, SDKs and runtime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish release criteria, test coverage expectations, defect management and regression processes, aligned with CI/CD practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring in secure development and software supply chain practice, including SBOMs and vulnerability management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support responsible AI and AI management practice where customers ask for it, including awareness of ISO/IEC 42001.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the senior point of contact for customer quality, audits and escalations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead customer RMA and complaint handling, root cause analysis and 8D responses to agreed timelines.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure product compliance with RoHS, REACH, WEEE, conflict minerals reporting, UKCA and CE marking, and relevant safety and EMC standards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential experience and skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in quality roles in semiconductors or electronics hardware, including creating and leading a quality function or team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience managing quality through outsourced manufacturing: foundries, OSATs, test houses and/or contract manufacturers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of ISO 9001 and hands-on experience building or running a certified QMS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of semiconductor qualification and reliability (JEDEC), failure analysis and</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awareness of data centre RAS assessments and HPC system qualification and certification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in core quality tools: 8D, FMEA, control plans, SPC, MSA and root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling customer quality escalations with large, demanding customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in electrical or electronic engineering, materials science, physics or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, confident communicator who can influence engineers, suppliers and executives, and hold partners to account.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willing to travel internationally, including to Asia and US, for supplier audits and customer quality reviews.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a fabless company, particularly one bringing an initial product to volume.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in high-performance compute, data centre, networking or AI hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to software quality, release management or secure development practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead auditor certification (ISO 9001), Six Sigma Black Belt, or chartered status (for example CQI or IET).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with suppliers in Taiwan, South Korea or US.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The impact you will have</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will help Fractile to makes sure every one of our suppliers builds to our standard, and that our customers receive AI hardware and software they can trust in production whilst shaping the quality culture across engineering, operations and commercial teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>What We Offer</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary: A competitive salary reflective of your experience and the specialist nature of the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity &amp; Ownership: meaningful equity so everyone shares in the value creation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits: Private Medical, Dental and Vision, Contributory Pension, 25 Days holiday plus bank holidays and Life/Critical Illness Insurance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diverse &amp; fun office: we believe the hardest problems get solved by the broadest range of minds. We are committed to Equal 