equires engineering systems that operate across software, hardware, and physical environments, and that remain reliable as scale and complexity increase.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are scaling our engineering organisation now. Most of our engineering manager seats are open. You join, shape how the teams work, and grow with them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Engineering Manager, you lead a team building and operating core parts of Radiant's cloud platform. You combine people leadership, technical judgement, delivery ownership and cross-functional collaboration. You work closely with product, infrastructure, SRE, security and other engineering teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on leadership role. It focuses on building strong teams, delivering reliable platform capabilities, and creating an environment where engineers do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The streams</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We run engineering as ten streams in three groups. Each stream is a full team of about nine people: principal, senior and mid-level software engineers, an SDET, a DevOps engineer and a platform engineer. Each stream has its own engineering manager.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infrastructure: Compute, Network, Storage, Cluster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Platform: Cloud, Infra, Observability, Security</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI: Training, Inference</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not apply for a single stream. We hire strong managers first. Then we agree your stream with you, based on your strengths and interests. Your first stream is a starting point, not a fixed track. Moves between streams are normal here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead one stream end to end: people, delivery and production.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach and develop a team of about nine engineers across platform, infrastructure and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own team execution across planning, prioritisation, delivery, quality and operational readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with product to turn priorities into clear technical plans and achievable milestones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical leadership on architecture, reliability, scalability and engineering trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set strong engineering practices for design, testing, observability, documentation and incident learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve team effectiveness through clear ownership, healthy processes and strong cross-team collaboration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard and retain high-performing engineers. Hiring is a large part of the first year. Expect around two hours a day on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support career development through regular feedback, coaching and progression planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage technical risk, dependencies and delivery challenges across complex platform initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring AI-assisted engineering into daily work, within our guardrails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a culture of ownership, pragmatism, operational excellence and continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Attitude comes first</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity: you learn new domains fast. GPUs, networks and storage excite you rather than worry you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candour: you say what you think, with care. You welcome challenge to your own ideas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builder mindset: much here is not built yet. You enjoy creating the process, not just running it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pace with standards: you move fast and keep quality high.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generosity: you make the people around you better. You give credit and share what you know.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading engineering teams building cloud platforms, infrastructure, developer tooling or distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong technical background. You engage credibly in architecture and design discussions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud infrastructure: compute, storage, networking, Kubernetes, containers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Platform engineering: APIs, automation, IAM, observability, reliability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Distributed systems: scaling, consistency, failure handling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering operations: incident response, capacity, performance, production ownership</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in people management, hiring, coaching and performance development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong delivery and prioritisation skills across competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working closely with product and other engineering leaders in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to balance technical quality, delivery speed, reliability and team sustainability.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with GPU, HPC or AI infrastructure is a bonus. Nobody has depth in every area above. Tell us which you know and which you want to learn.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul styl