ove logistics and get the new office set up and running from day one</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee, Visitor &amp; New Hire Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the primary on-site point of contact for employees, visitors, candidates, and vendors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the office for new hire start days, partnering with People on onboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and run London events, socials, offsites, and all-hands logistics, including catering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the on-site IT point of contact and manage equipment inventory</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3-5 years of experience in workplace, office management, or facilities, ideally at a fast-growing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with an office move, fit-out, or new office opening preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable managing vendors, budgets, and several projects at once</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organised, proactive, and comfortable working independently with a manager based in NYC</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Warm, professional presence: you take pride in creating a great experience for everyone who walks through the door</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with UK health and safety requirements is a plus</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You thrive in fast-paced environments. </strong>You are high-intensity and care a lot about what you do, and you're ecstatic to work at a startup. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You are ambitious. </strong>You have fun solving problems that others think are