ull potential.<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover" href="https://alan.com/en/blog/discover-alan/a/alan-culture-excellence-through-coaching"><strong>Learn more about our coaching culture</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental leave</strong>. Extended parental leave for all new parents, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Important note: we hire people, not roles.</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about this opportunity but don't check every box, <strong>we'd love to hear from you.</strong> Everyone, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply as it can only bring learnings or success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If you identify yourself as a woman</strong>: Did you know that research shows women often apply only when meeting 100% of requirements?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remember, this is just a guide, not a checklist.</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'll be thrilled to receive your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔖 Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/about">About Alan</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/careers">Career</a> pages, as well as our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/alan">Medium</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.alan.com/">blog</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm">Glassdoor page</a> for more info.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alan/enterprise-account-executive-paris-france-383149","tags":["Sales 🇫🇷"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1792129217},{"slug":"social-media-content-specialist-anywhere-in-france-201418","company_name":"Alan","title":"Social Media & Content Specialist","description":"<h2><strong>Health can’t wait</strong>. </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not for symptoms to get worse. Not for a six‑month appointment. Not for a system to catch up. But that’s exactly how healthcare works today. You wait, until you can’t.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan exists to end the wait.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health is a universal right, and we believe this right can only become real when it’s coupled with prevention. We need to stop treating health as something we repair and start treating it as something we build, every day. It’s not solely a question of willpower. It’s the healthcare system itself that needs to work for everyone, in a sustainable way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">So we are building the<strong> new standard in prevention insurance. </strong>Alan is the first company that integrates insurance, prevention, and care into a single, acclaimed user experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are on an incredible journey to build a <strong>global leading company, with a </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers"><strong><u>unique culture</u></strong></a>. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><h1><strong>⭐ The role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health is one of the most searched, shared and talked-about topics online. Millions of people scroll every day looking for answers about their sleep, their stress or their kids' fever. And yet, no brand owns that conversation. We want Alan to be the health voice people actually want to follow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Social Media &amp; Content Specialist , you'll be the owner of Alan's organic social presence in France (Instagram, LinkedIn, YouTube…)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join the Brand team and work side by side with an experienced content editorial team</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you’ll own</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The France editorial line. </strong>Build and run the editorial calendar, content pillars (prevention, health tips, product, employer brand…) and posting cadence for each platform. Work with Brand, Product Marketing, Medical and Growth teams to pull the best stories, data and expertise from across Alan, and turn them into content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Content creation</strong>. Create and ship social-first content yourself, every week: short videos (Reels, Shorts), carousels, statics and copy-led LinkedIn posts. You write the hooks, the scripts and the captions, you edit the videos and you design the visuals. You adapt each piece to its platform rather than posting the same thing everywhere.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Alan's voice on social</strong>. Define how Alan sounds on social: credible on health, but human, useful and sometimes funny. Spot the news, trends and formats worth jumping on, and react at the right moment, in the right tone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Alan's big moments</strong>. Plan and run the social side of brand campaigns, product launches and events, from the idea to the publication, so that every major moment gets the reach it deserves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Community.</strong> Reply to comments and messages, moderate, spark conversations, and collaborate with Alan experts (doctors, psychologists…), employees and creators to grow an engaged audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance</strong>. Follow the analytics, run regular test-and-learn on formats, hooks and timing, and share a simple monthly review with the team. Work with Growth and Data to track what social brings to Alan (traffic, awareness, audience quality).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI in the creative and distribution process</strong>. Use AI tools to create more, faster and better, and help us shape how AI fits into our content production and distribution workflow, with the support of our engineers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who we’re looking for</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You create. </strong>You still open the tools yourself (CapCut, Premiere, Figma, Canva, AI tools…) and love making content. You don't brief others to do it for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You live and breathe social</strong>. You get the trends, the memes and the codes of each platform, and you know when (and when not) to jump in.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You have taste and a pen.</strong> You write sharp, punchy copy and can tell a strong idea from a weak one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You take ownership. </strong>You go and get the information you need, make decisions, ship at the right moment and follow through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're data-minded.</strong> You care about what a post changed, not just the likes, and use the numbers to decide what's next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're scrappy and curious.</strong> You make great content, and you're always testing new formats, platform features and tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You collaborate</strong>. You make it easy and fun for people across Alan to contribute to social, and you're energised by a blank page.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Requirements for the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You may be a great fit if you’ve:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2–5 years of hands-on social media experience </strong>(brand, media or agency side), with at least one account you owned or co-owned</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio of content you created yourself, across formats (short video, carousels, copy)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience on at least two of <strong>Instagram, YouTube and LinkedIn</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>French fluent level,</strong> with flawless written French: most of the content will be in French</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced <strong>written and verbal communication</strong> skills in <strong>English</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spanish or Dutch is a plus, given Alan's presence in Spain and Belgium</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in <strong>France</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the<strong> B1-C1</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"><u>level range</u></a>.</p><h1><br />🙌   <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/about/life-at-alan/a/perks">Perks &amp; Benefits</a></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Alan, we believe that <strong>being in good health is a basic need</strong>, and it starts with our employees. This is why Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are <strong>happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time</strong> with co-workers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Therefore, we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fair rewards</strong>. Generous equity packages complement your base salary, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible office with hybrid setup</strong>. Amazing office space at our Paris HQ or sponsored co-working hubs in Bordeaux, Marseille, Lyon, Annecy, Nantes or Biarritz.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All the tools you need</strong>. Top of the range equipment: Macbook Air, keyboard, laptop stand, monitor, and Bose noise-canceling headphones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible vacation policy and flexible working hours</strong>. Organize your time as you wish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delightful healthcare insurance:</strong> Extremely comprehensive health insurance - 100% for you and your children, 90-100% for partners depending on your country<em> (permanent contracts only).</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transport</strong>. Generous transit benefit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Training opportunities</strong>. A highly flexible training policy free books and budget to attend and speak at conferences if the opportunity arises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth through coaching</strong>: At Alan, coaching isn't just a perk - it's core to who we are. Every Alaner is paired with a dedicated coach from day one, who helps maximize their impact, nurture engagement, and navigate Alan's values to develop their full potential.<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover" href="https://alan.com/en/blog/discover-alan/a/alan-culture-excellence-through-coaching"><strong>Learn more about our coaching culture</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental leave</strong>. Extended parental leave for all new parents, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>🎯 Important note: we hire people, not roles</strong>.</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about this opportunity but don't check every box, we'd love to hear from you. Everyone, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply, as it can only bring learnings or success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you identify yourself as a woman: Did you know that research shows women often apply only when meeting 100% of requirements?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remember, this is just a guide, not a checklist. We'll be thrilled to receive your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔖 Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/about"><u>About Alan</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/careers"><u>Career</u></a> pages, as well as our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/alan"><u>Medium</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.alan.com/"><u>blog</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm"><u>Glassdoor page</u></a> for more info.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alan/social-media-content-specialist-anywhere-in-france-201418","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Anywhere in France","created_at":1792129217},{"slug":"ingenieur-rd-conception-dequipements-dessais-h-f-lyon-454240","company_name":"Inautalent","title":"Ingénieur R&D Conception d'équipements d’essais (H/F)","description":"<h3><strong>Ingénieur R&amp;D Conception d'équipements d’essais&nbsp; (H/F)</strong></h3><h3></h3><p><strong>À propos de notre client</strong></p><p>Notre client est une TPE basée au nord de Lyon, spécialisée dans les énergies du sous-sol : pétrole, gaz, géothermie et stockage de CO2. Son activité repose entièrement sur la R&amp;D : essais sur géomatériaux, géomécanique et développement d'équipements d'essais pour des clients internationaux.</p><p>Son équipe pluridisciplinaire et multiculturelle développe des solutions technologiques innovantes au service de l'efficacité, de la protection de l'environnement et de la maîtrise des coûts. L'entreprise est certifiée ISO 9001 et toutes ses activités respectent sa démarche QHSE.</p><p></p><p><strong>Le poste</strong></p><p>Pour accélérer ses projets de développement, notre client recrute un(e) Ingénieur(e) R&amp;D en conception d'équipements d'essais.&nbsp; Vous prendrez en charge la conception, la mise au point et la validation de cellules d'essais haute température et haute pression, un sujet stratégique pour l'entreprise et ses clients.</p><p>Rattaché(e) à la direction des opérations, vous travaillerez en étroite collaboration avec l'équipe qui conçoit aujourd'hui les équipements et dépose les brevets de l'entreprise.</p><p>Répartition indicative du temps : environ 70 à 80 % conception et développement, 20 à 30 % laboratoire (montage et validation de vos équipements).</p><p>Dans une structure à taille humaine, vous suivrez vos développements de la conception jusqu'aux tests, avant leur transfert à l'équipe de production.</p><p></p><p><strong>Vos missions</strong></p><p>Conception et développement d'équipements d’essais</p><ul><li>Concevoir de nouvelles cellules et de nouveaux dispositifs d'essais, notamment pour des conditions de haute température et de haute pression.</li><li>Résoudre les problématiques techniques associées : instrumentation et capteurs, étanchéité, tenue en température et en pression.</li><li>Consulter les fournisseurs et sous-traitants, et suivre la fabrication des pièces.</li><li>Améliorer les équipements existants, notamment leur ergonomie et leur facilité d'utilisation en production.</li></ul><p>Mise au point et validation</p><ul><li>Monter les équipements développés et réaliser leurs tests de validation au laboratoire.</li><li>Interpréter les résultats expérimentaux et vérifier leur cohérence.</li><li>Transférer les équipements validés à l'équipe de production et l'accompagner dans leur prise en main.</li></ul><p>Documentation et propriété intellectuelle</p><ul><li>Rédiger la documentation technique, les rapports et les comptes-rendus, et les présenter, en français comme en anglais.</li><li>Participer à la veille technique et à la rédaction des documents de protection (brevets, enveloppes Soleau).</li></ul><p>Vie du laboratoire</p><ul><li>Comprendre les essais réalisés au laboratoire pour concevoir des équipements adaptés à leurs besoins.</li><li>Contribuer à l'activité du labo et à l'amélioration continue, dans le respect de la démarche qualité ISO 9001.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p>Compétences techniques</p><ul><li>Conception mécanique et maîtrise d'un logiciel de CAO.</li><li>Instrumentation, capteurs et techniques de mesure.</li><li>Compréhension des grandeurs physiques et physico-chimiques.</li><li>Rédaction technique et anglais professionnel, à l'oral comme à l'écrit.</li></ul><p></p><p>Savoir-être</p><ul><li>Autonomie et capacité à prendre en main un sujet de bout en bout.</li><li>Rigueur, notamment dans les phases d'essais.</li><li>Polyvalence et goût du concret : vous aimez concevoir autant que tester vous-même vos équipements.</li><li>Communication proactive, en particulier pour remonter et résoudre les difficultés rencontrées.</li><li>Envie d'apprendre et de s'investir dans une petite structure.</li></ul><p></p><p>Formation et expérience</p><ul><li>Diplôme d'ingénieur ou équivalent Bac +5 en génie mécanique, conception, instrumentation ou mesures physiques.</li><li>Expérience d'environ 5 ans en conception d'équipements, en bureau d'études ou en R&amp;D. Les profils plus juniors avec une première expérience significative en conception seront étudiés.</li><li>Une expérience sur des équipements soumis à des contraintes de température ou de pression est un vrai plus.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p>Vous rejoindrez une entreprise à taille humaine où chaque développement compte : vos équipements seront directement utilisés pour des projets de R&amp;D menés pour des clients internationaux. Vous travaillerez au sein d'une équipe dynamique et multiculturelle, sur des sujets techniques exigeants au service des énergies du sous-sol et de la transition énergétique.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/inautalent/ingenieur-rd-conception-dequipements-dessais-h-f-lyon-454240","tags":["Research"],"job_types":["Full time","associate"],"location":"Lyon, France","created_at":1792124414},{"slug":"ingenieur-rd-conception-dequipements-dessais-h-f-neuville-sur-saone-216884","company_name":"Inautalent","title":"Ingénieur R&D Conception d'équipements d’essais (H/F)","description":"<h3><strong>Ingénieur R&amp;D Conception d'équipements d’essais&nbsp; (H/F)</strong></h3><h3></h3><p><strong>À propos de notre client</strong></p><p>Notre client est une TPE basée au nord de Lyon, spécialisée dans les énergies du sous-sol : pétrole, gaz, géothermie et stockage de CO2. Son activité repose entièrement sur la R&amp;D : essais sur géomatériaux, géomécanique et développement d'équipements d'essais pour des clients internationaux.</p><p>Son équipe pluridisciplinaire et multiculturelle développe des solutions technologiques innovantes au service de l'efficacité, de la protection de l'environnement et de la maîtrise des coûts. L'entreprise est certifiée ISO 9001 et toutes ses activités respectent sa démarche QHSE.</p><p></p><p><strong>Le poste</strong></p><p>Pour accélérer ses projets de développement, notre client recrute un(e) Ingénieur(e) R