<li><strong>Support HRBPs in their day-to-day decisions.</strong> Translate their questions into relevant analyses, discuss which KPIs are most useful, and help them become more autonomous through documentation and practical guidance.</li>
<li><strong>Contribute to workforce and talent analyses.</strong> Prepare datasets, reports, and analytical inputs for topics such as headcount planning, compensation reviews, and talent reviews, in collaboration with the team.</li>
<li><strong>Use AI to improve how you work.</strong> Apply AI to relevant analytical and reporting tasks, test practical ways to save time, and check the accuracy and reliability of outputs.</li>
</ul>
<h2>➡️ What we’re looking for</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Relevant experience</strong> in People Analytics, HR reporting, or a data analytics role with substantial exposure to HR topics, ideally within a tech company or scale-up. <strong>A solid understanding of HR processes.</strong> Compensation reviews, talent reviews, and HRBP activities are familiar territory. You understand the questions behind a reporting request and can discuss whether a metric addresses them.</li>
<li><strong>Hands-on analytical skills.</strong> You’re comfortable using SQL, Excel, and BI tools to combine datasets, check calculations, investigate trends, and build clear dashboards. Experience with HRIS reporting, particularly Workday, is a plus.</li>
<li><strong>Clear communication and sound judgment.</strong> You can explain findings to non-technical stakeholders, ask useful questions, and distinguish what the data supports from what still needs investigating. <strong>Reliable delivery and collaborative working habits.</strong> You can progress independently on defined analyses, keep stakeholders informed, and flag blockers or competing priorities early.</li>
<li><strong>Practical experience using AI.</strong> You already use AI in your work and can explain where it improves your efficiency or output quality, how you verify results, and how you protect sensitive information.</li>
<li><strong>Professional fluency in English.</strong> French is a strong plus.</li>
</ul>
<h2>➡️ What we can offer you</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Meaningful analytical work</strong> that helps the People team understand workforce trends and make better-informed decisions.</li>
<li><strong>Varied HR topics</strong>, from performance and attrition to compensation, workforce planning, and reporting.</li>
