 HR, Legal and Finance, working together to drive Voodoo’s success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a <strong>Legal Counsel, AdTech Transactions</strong> to join our Legal team. In this role, you'll own the contracts and legal questions across Voodoo's advertising activity: selling ad inventory in our apps, buying user acquisition at scale, and the ad network we are now launching to connect third-party publishers and advertisers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This position sits at the intersection of ad tech, commercial contracting, and data and privacy law, in a market where platform policies, ATT, GDPR, and consent frameworks change several times a year. Your work will directly shape how Voodoo monetizes its inventory, buys and measures user acquisition, grows its advertising network, and handles player data,while keeping us within legal and platform requirements and player expectations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main responsibilities :</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own ad tech transactions end-to-end for Voodoo's games and apps portfolio: draft, negotiate and close agreements with mediation platforms, ad networks, exchanges and SSPs on the sell side, and with ad networks, DSPs, direct advertisers and rewarded platforms on the buy side,including the incentive and rebate agreements (bonuses, UA credits, payment terms), that drive the commercial terms..</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate agreements with mobile measurement partners, attribution and analytics vendors, data providers and other partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on SDK integrations and data flows together with the Privacy team, so contracts match what the tech actually does</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build our advertising network's contract framework and advertising policies for third-party publishers, advertisers and programmatic partners; negotiate its infrastructure agreements and structure its commercial offers on the legal side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage partner disputes with networks, mediation platforms and other ad tech partners, including reporting discrepancies, invalid traffic (IVT) and compensation claims, from first analysis through negotiated resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and apply platform policy changes and translate them into contract positions and business guidance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate cross-functionally with Monetization, UA, Ad Network, Publishing and other product teams, serving as a trusted legal partner who helps the business move with speed and confidence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build scalable legal infrastructure-templates, playbooks, fallback positions, contract tooling - that allows the business to operate efficiently as volume grows</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Profile</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5-7 years of relevant legal experience, with meaningful time spent on ad tech and mobile/programmatic advertising, ideally in-house</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantive familiarity with ad tech: you understand how mediation, in-app bidding, SDK-based data collection, attribution and device identifiers work at a technical level - not just a conceptual one - and you know who does what along the supply chain</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transactional experience: you've negotiated agreements with companies across the advertising ecosystem, ideally on both the publisher and advertiser side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Privacy law fluency: you handle the privacy side of a deal as comfortably as the commercial side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Industry standards: you know IAB terms and the TCF inside out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Risk tolerance and business judgment: you're comfortable making calls in the absence of perfect information, offering clear and concise risk framing that avoids unnecessary stalling of the business. You operate like a business partner, not outside counsel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills: you translate complex legal requirements into plain language for technical and non-technical stakeholders alike, and you're comfortable presenting your views succinctly and with confidence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomy and initiative: you take ownership of your portfolio, identify problems before they escalate, and propose solutions rather than waiting to be directed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master 2 in business law, IT/digital law or IP law from a French university or equivalent; avocat or in-house juriste profiles are equally welcome; an LL.M. or study abroad experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full professional English required</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Benefits</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Swile Lunch voucher</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gymlib (100% covered by Voodoo)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Premium healthcare coverage with SideCare, 100% covered for you and your family</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellness activities in our Paris office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote Fridays</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/voodoo/legal-counsel-adtech-transactions-paris-386443","tags":["Corporate"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792096816},{"slug":"support-engineer-last-mile-delivery-lille-upline-nord-4609","company_name":"Decathlontechnology","title":"Support Engineer - Last Mile Delivery (f/m/d)","description":"&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Notre équipe Ship &amp;amp; Back recherche un·e Support Engineer (f/m/d) en CDI basé·e à Lille.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de la Value Chain de Decathlon, l&#39;équipe Last Mile Delivery propulse l&#39;expérience sportive au niveau supérieur en garantissant une livraison fluide, rapide et fiable partout dans le monde. Composée d&#39;une dizaine de passionné·es du produit et de la tech, notre mission est d&#39;optimiser le cœur battant de la logistique e-commerce à travers 3 produits clés : Shipperbox (tracking et étiquettes transporteurs), RPM (référentiel des points relais) et Trackbox (assure la livraison des commandes e-commerce, leur suivi et leur performance). En rejoignant notre équipe à taille humaine, tu prendras le lead du support fonctionnel sur un périmètre stratégique, avec l&#39;ambition de garantir une performance de livraison sans faille pour des millions d&#39;utilisateur·rices.&lt;/p&gt;
