&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/decathlontechnology/mobile-device-management-unified-endpoint-management-ops-engineer-lille-btwin-village-nord-paris-paris-54141","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":[],"location":"Lille - Btwin Village, Nord; Paris, Paris","created_at":1792086918},{"slug":"senior-solutions-engineer-french-speaker-paris-363255","company_name":"Synthesia","title":"Senior Solutions Engineer - French Speaker","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesia is the world’s leading AI video platform for business, used by over 90% of the Fortune 100. Founded in 2017, the company is headquartered in London, with offices and teams across Europe and the US. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI continues to shape the way we live and work, Synthesia develops products to enhance visual communication and enterprise skill development, helping people work better and stay at the center of successful organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Following our recent Series E funding round, where we raised $200 million, our valuation stands at $4 billion. Our total funding exceeds $530 million from premier investors including Accel, NVentures (Nvidia's VC arm), Kleiner Perkins, GV, and Evantic Capital, alongside the founders and operators of Stripe, Datadog, Miro, and Webflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a Senior Solutions Engineer to build Synthesia’s presales function in France and Southern EMEA. This is a founding role: you’ll be one of the first SEs, shaping the playbook, tooling and best practices as we scale, not following an established model. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Solutions Engineer at Synthesia, you will partner with Account Executives, Customer Success and Product Marketing to run discovery, deliver demos, scope POCs and design the technical solution for each deal. You will be a trusted advisor focused on the value customers get from Synthesia, and you’ll take what you learn in the field back to Product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an incredible opportunity to join us as we become a multi-product company for the first time, and continue to scale across France and Southern EMEA. If you’re someone who is excited and driven by building whilst scaling, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Sales Cycle Ownership</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coplan and execute discovery calls to understand customer requirements, their technical environment, and current business challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver compelling demonstrations that solve customer problems, quantify the value of solving those problems, and tell a clear, credible story of how Synthesia solves them better than anything else.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand and overcome technical objections and integration concerns; identify blockers early and develop solution paths with customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support stakeholder workshops that connect Synthesia to the buyer's broader technology strategy on complex, multi-stakeholder deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Account Executives to define account and deal strategy, advise on competitive positioning, and provide your assessment of opportunity stage and forecast your book of business to leadership.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Demo Excellence</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute repeatable Demo methodologies that prove Synthesia’s business value quickly, whether the customer is deploying Studio at scale, designing Roleplay Sessions for skill uplift, or integrating Interactive Avatars into their product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify, build relationships with, and actively empower executive champions within customer organizations so they can advocate for Synthesia internally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain reusable assets across demo environments, use cases, integration templates, objections, and industry playbooks brought to life directly in Synthesia’s platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support POC and pilot readouts as a business narrative, not a feature tour, learning to bring storytelling and executive presence to the room as you grow into more senior conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical guidance on platform capabilities, API and SDK integrations, security, compliance topics (SOC 2, GDPR, enterprise identity), and scalability for global deployments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Product &amp; Industry Expertise</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain deep expertise on Synthesia's platform capabilities across all product lines, roadmap, and positioning to highlight value driving use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specific vertical knowledge, establishing credibility as a subject matter expert within an industry to easily build credibility and trust with executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share customer and prospect product and competitive feedback to the pre-sales leadership and Product team; flag customer pain points, missing capabilities, and gaps that surface in live deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay ahead of the AI-native learning and enablement space, so you can credibly discuss how customers are shifting from current, static methods to interactive practice and measurable skill development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Ecosystem Collaboration</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product: </strong>share customer and prospect feedback with Product, flagging pain points, missing capabilities, and gaps that surface in your deals to help shape the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Marketing: </strong>work with Product Marketing to understand and apply messaging and positioning in your deal cycles, and contribute to reusable assets like demo scripts and competitive battlecards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Success: </strong>brief Customer Success on technical context and champion relationships at handover, so your POCs and pilots convert cleanly into production deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enablement: </strong>Review and enhance enablement content from what is effective in preparing our team members for client engagements, delivering and evaluating certification as needed to accelerate understanding in the commercial team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We think the ideal candidate for this role will bring 5+ years of pre-sales, solutions engineering, or customer-facing technical experience at SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong consultative discovery, stakeholder management, and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with both executive decision-makers (CHRO, CLO, Head of L&amp;D, CTO) and technical audiences (IT, security, developers).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical depth in at least one area: Creation flows, APIs, integrations (LMS, HCM, CRM, identity), security, compliance; willingness to learn quickly across domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency with sales methodologies such as MEDDPICC and Command of the Message. Comfort translating technical requirements into business value and ROI conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consultative approach to problem-solving; comfort gathering requirements, asking clarifying questions, and adapting solutions to customer needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent business and technical presentation skills, in person and remote, and the ability to explain complex AI and integration concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated and organized; ability to manage multiple POCs, demos, and customer conversations simultaneously while meeting deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative mindset; thrives working with AEs, Product, Customer Success, and other teams to drive customer and company success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product orientation; genuine curiosity about how customers use technology</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willing to travel; willingness to visit key customers for discovery, executive conversations, and on-site demos.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re ideally looking for someone based in Paris who can spend time in our office at 40 Rue du Colisée, 75008 Paris, or someone based in the UK who can spend time in our London office at 20 Triton Street, Regent’s Place, London NW1 3BF. Please confirm where you are located and whether you can spend two days a week in either location. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/synthesia/senior-solutions-engineer-french-speaker-paris-363255","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792086021},{"slug":"associate-director-director-customer-engagement-international-zug-390253","company_name":"Bridgebio","title":"Associate Director/ Director Customer Engagement, International","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Senior Director Commercial Excellence, International and work closely with country teams, International commercial functions, IT, and Corporate Communications to drive strategic initiatives that support BridgeBio’s mission of delivering transformative medicines to patients with genetic diseases and genetically driven cancers. Your primary purpose will be to build and own the International omnichannel customer engagement strategy, including digital and social activities across International markets. This role requires effective collaboration with cross-functional colleagues and external stakeholders to ensure high-quality execution and impact. The ideal candidate combines deep expertise in omnichannel and digital customer engagement with strong communication skills, adaptability, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, hands-on environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the International omnichannel customer engagement strategy across HCPs and patients, designing customer journeys and defining channel mix, sequencing, and engagement across personal and digital touchpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Sales Force Effectiveness to embed omnichannel plans into CRM, field execution, and next best action, and advise country teams and customer-facing functions on effective use of engagement tools and content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the International digital channel landscape, including disease-awareness websites, HCP portals, email and marketing automation, and paid and organic social media, setting the website strategy, content roadmap, and social media governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set content operations standards, including modular content requirements and localization guardrails, and own the omnichannel requirements for the CRM and digital tech infrastructure in partnership with CommEx and IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the International omnichannel measurement plan, defining KPIs and generating actionable insights from campaign, channel, and CRM data, and champion innovative approaches to customer engagement, including AI and large language model applications, piloting new tools in a compliant and measurable way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct and quality-check the delivery of pilot campaigns and ecosystem-build work against the channel plan and standards, and manage digital agencies and technology vendors supporting omnichannel delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an office-based role in our Zug, Switzerland office, requiring in-office collaboration 2-3x per week, with additional travel of up to 20% across International markets to support country teams, congresses, and launch readiness&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA or BS in Business, Life Sciences, or a related field; MBA or other advanced degree/certification preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10+ years of experience in the Pharmaceutical/Biotech industry, including experience in omnichannel, digital, or customer engagement roles, supporting product launches (specialty or rare disease strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing and executing omnichannel customer engagement strategies across multiple markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with digital channels and platforms, including websites, email and marketing automation, and social media, together with CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of change management and driving adoption of new channels, processes, and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced analytical and strategic skills, with the ability to turn engagement and campaign data into clear decisions and recommendations; experience in a lean or growth-stage organization preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to multiple geographies strongly preferred, with deep expertise in at least one region required; fluency in English required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
