&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/bridgebio/associate-director-director-customer-engagement-international-zug-390253","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zug","created_at":1791989748},{"slug":"young-graduate-in-data-and-software-engineering-zurich-switzerland-zurich-364046","company_name":"Unit8","title":"Young Graduate in Data and Software Engineering (Zurich, Switzerland)","description":"<p><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p>Founded in 2017, Unit8 is a fast-growing Swiss AI and data analytics consulting and services company dedicated to solving complex problems of traditional industries like automotive, chemical, financial services, manufacturing and pharma. We work with some of the biggest organizations in Europe to solve the challenges that directly affect their business - be it operations, finance, manufacturing or R&amp;D. Since our foundation, we have successfully delivered more than 300 projects and have grown to 190+ talented individuals across 10 office locations.</p><p><br>Unit8’s mission is to drive the adoption of AI and Data Science in the non-digital industries and to help accelerate their digital transformation. Among its activities, Unit8 dedicates a part of its resources and time on projects that deeply matter to us - that includes collaboration on pro-bono and “engineering for good” causes.<br></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p><strong>Unit8</strong> is welcoming young graduates for the opportunity to grow in <strong>Data and Software Engineering! </strong>Join us for a 6-month paid professional experience in building industrial Data and AI solutions. You can start asap, with direct exposure to clients' needs and opportunities to participate in learning activities such as Reading Groups and Knowledge Sharing Sessions. In addition, each young graduate will be accompanied by a dedicated wingmate/mentor who will guide and help them build their technical growth vision.</p><p><br>As a young graduate you will join a team of Data Scientists, Data Engineers and Cloud Engineers who work hand-in-hand with our customers on designing and implementing their industry-specific use cases. You will be directly involved in discussing the client’s challenges and needs and will have chances to develop your client-facing skills. You will be responsible for developing, deploying, and automating our AI services and cloud infrastructure. You will also learn to carefully analyse a given problem and apply the relevant tools and techniques to solve it.<br></p><p><strong>In general you will:</strong></p><ul><li>use software best practices in continuous integration and delivery, versioning and automation;</li><li>use your skills to build and maintain service and data infrastructure;</li><li>participate as junior engineer in all phases of the software development life cycle - planning, implementation, deployment, testing and maintenance;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Are You the team member we are looking for?</strong></p><p>In order to be successful in this role, you are/have:</p><ul><li>motivated and eager to learn different aspects of engineering</li><li>comfortable interacting with technical and business people</li><li>strong communication and presentation skills</li><li>recently graduated/finishing your MSc or BSc in Computer Science or related major;</li><li>familiar with version control and collaboration tooling (git)</li><li>familiar with CI/CD frameworks and automated deployment concepts (i.e Docker, K8s)</li><li>fluent in both <strong>English</strong> and <strong>German</strong></li><li>available for a minimum of 32h a week.</li><li><strong>ready to start on the 1st of February </strong></li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul><li>Exposure to a wide variety of projects, industries, and technologies. Each client is different and provides unique opportunities to learn. </li><li>Ability to contribute to internal open-source projects like Darts (<a href="https://github.com/unit8co/darts" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">https://github.com/unit8co/darts</a>) </li><li>Learning activities such as ML Reading Group, knowledge sharing sessions with engineers.</li><li>Training-on-the-job and your personal wingmate/mentor</li><li>15 paid days of holiday</li><li>Be part of an international team of more than 20 nationalities.</li><li>up to 10% of paid time for self-development.</li><li>Flexible working hours, including some home office.</li><li>Cross offices/company-wide frequent events like offsites.</li><li>If you are successful, opportunity to be then hired for a permanent position.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/unit8/young-graduate-in-data-and-software-engineering-zurich-switzerland-zurich-364046","tags":["Engineering","Information Technology and Services"],"job_types":["Full time","internship"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1791987612},{"slug":"remote-palantir-foundry-engineer-relocation-to-abu-dhabi-uae-lausanne-52118","company_name":"Unit8","title":"Palantir Foundry Engineer (Relocation to Abu Dhabi, UAE)","description":"<h3><strong>Who We Are</strong></h3><p>Founded in 2017, Unit8 is a Swiss data and AI consulting company helping organisations in traditional industries solve complex challenges in areas such as operations, finance, manufacturing and R&amp;D. We work at the intersection of technology and business, delivering data and AI solutions that create practical value for our clients.</p><p>Our teams have delivered projects across industries including automotive, chemicals, financial services, manufacturing and pharma. We are a Palantir partner and work with clients across the full data and AI journey, from understanding a business problem to building and deploying the solution.</p><p>Unit8 has delivered more than 300 projects and grown to a team of 190+ talented people across ten office locations. Following our growth across Europe and our expansion into North America, we are now building our presence in the United Arab Emirates. We are looking for a Palantir Foundry Engineer to join us in Abu Dhabi. This role is based in the UAE and includes relocation from Switzerland with full immigration and relocation support.</p><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3>About the Role</h3><p>As one of the first members of Unit8’s team in the UAE, you will help deliver Foundry solutions for clients while contributing to the growth of our presence in the region.</p><p>You will work directly with client teams to understand their data and operational challenges, then design and build solutions that address them. The role combines hands-on engineering with close collaboration across business and technical teams. You will also contribute your technical perspective during early client discussions and help shape practical approaches to new opportunities.</p><p></p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul><li>Design, build, deploy and maintain data solutions using Palantir Foundry.</li><li>Develop and troubleshoot data pipelines and processing systems using Foundry and relevant open-source or proprietary technologies.</li><li>Build and maintain Foundry components such as Ontologies, pipelines, and user-facing applications.</li><li>Apply sound engineering practices for testing, data quality, performance, security and maintainability.</li><li>Work with client stakeholders to understand requirements, clarify problems and translate business needs into technical solutions.</li><li>Collaborate with engineers, data scientists, product owners and client teams in an agile environment.</li><li>Contribute to technical discovery and solution scoping for prospective and ongoing engagements.</li><li>Help establish Unit8’s engineering and delivery approach in the UAE, sharing knowledge with colleagues and supporting the growth of the local team.</li></ul><p></p><h3><strong>About You</strong></h3><p>We are looking for an experienced <strong>Palantir</strong> <strong>Foundry Engineer</strong> with a passion for data and solving complex client challenges. You should be a skilled professional who has:</p><p><strong>* Foundry Platform Knowledge </strong></p><ul><ul><li>Demonstrated experience with <strong>AIP, Workshop, Code repository, and Pipeline Builder</strong>.</li><li>A solid understanding of <strong>security concepts</strong> within Foundry, including restricted views and markings.</li><li>Knowledge of <strong>Ontology</strong> and <strong>Data connection</strong>.</li><li>We're interested in the technical details of what you've built and how you approached the architecture of your Foundry use-cases.</li></ul></ul><p><strong>* Programming Skills - </strong>proficiency in <strong>Python</strong> and <strong>PySpark</strong>.</p><p><strong>* Data Skills (Nice-to-have) - </strong>knowledge of <strong>data modeling</strong> and basic concepts of <strong>data science</strong> (classification, clustering, regression).</p><p><strong>* Professional Experience</strong></p><ul><li>A minimum of <strong>1 year of experience</strong> working with the Foundry platform, ideally within a larger company where you may have had a focused but deep exposure.</li><li> <strong>Strong client-facing skills:</strong> You are comfortable interacting with both business and technical clients, giving presentations, and possess a strong problem-solving mindset.</li></ul><p><strong>* Other</strong></p><ul><li>You are willing to travel to meet with our clients and the team</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><h3><strong>What We Offer</strong></h3><ul><li>The opportun