ation/heat tracing philosophy, cold start/commissioning constraints). You ensure the design is constructable and able to operate and be maintained through cold or hot conditions, including consideration of temporary works, for instance winter work sequencing, and interface constraints with cold-weather activities.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Professional Experience: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">You have a bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering or equivalent and have at least 10 years of experience in process plants various climates as an Electrical Engineer.&nbsp; You have experience leading teams.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Project Experience: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">You have hands-on involvement in at least one full-cycle project in the mining, water treatment, oil and gas or other comparable industries, covering all phases from FEED and detailed design to construction, commissioning and start-up; preferably in remote/seasonally constrained execution environments.&nbsp; You have expertise in low and medium voltage electrical systems, industrial instrumentation, and control systems.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Cold-Weather Industrial Plant Experience</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You have hands-on experience working with industrial plants in cold-weather environments (e.g. Canada, Nordic countries, or similar climates) and understand the operational, maintenance, and safety challenges associated with extreme weather conditions.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Communication &amp; Collaboration:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You demonstrate excellent written and verbal communication skills and can liaise with diverse stakeholders, including third-party vendors in IP-sensitive collaborations.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Working Style: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">You are precise, adaptable, and reliable, with a proactive and solution-oriented approach. You are comfortable driving decisions and owning them in the office and under field constraints, including winter productivity and schedule risk.&nbsp; You are highly organized, able to plan and prioritize work for yourself and others, and comfortable working in fast-paced environments.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Language Skills and Travel</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You are fluent in English and ready to travel up to 40% of your time (including extended site presence during peak design, engineering, construction and commissioning periods).</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Our promise:  </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">At Climeworks, you are accepted for who you are, and we are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone feels valued. We encourage </span><em><span style="color:#121317">all</span></em><span style="color:#121317"> qualified applicants to apply – regardless of background, identity, or experience. Studies show that women and individuals from minority backgrounds often only apply for jobs when they meet 100% of the listed criteria. If this sounds like you, don’t hold back. If you think you’d make a great fit for this role, we’d love to hear from you, even if you don’t check every single box. Let’s tackle one of humankind’s greatest challenges together.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">What we offer:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Time Off:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Enjoy 25 paid vacation days every year, plus public holidays.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Flexibility:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Work how it suits you best. We offer a hybrid work setup and up to 4 weeks of remote work annually within any EU country.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Ownership:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Fair base pay paired with an equity package – because your contributions matter.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Family Support:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Inclusive parental leave.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous Learning:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Dedicated budget to invest in your professional growth.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Referral Rewards:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Help us grow our team and earn bonuses for your successful referrals.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Salary: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">At Climeworks, salary ranges are assigned to a job based on the level of seniority and the location specific market median of similar jobs according to external benchmark surveys. Individual compensation depends on your skills, experience, and the value you bring to the team.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Formalities:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">This position is based in Opfikon, Zurich, and we ask that you work onsite at least three days per week.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">We do not accept candidate profiles through recruitment agencies.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/climeworks/lead-electrical-engineer-100-zurich-460857","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Senior manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Zurich, Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1791923425},{"slug":"consulting-partner-romandie-strategy-data-ai-transformation-lausanne-vaud-138562","company_name":"Artefact","title":"Consulting Partner Romandie (Strategy & Data/AI Transformation)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a global data and AI consulting firm. We help organisations turn data and AI into measurable business impact across the value chain, from strategy and operating model to data platforms, AI products and marketing. More than 2,500 consultants, data scientists and engineers work for over 1,000 clients worldwide, including Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Switzerland, our team of around 50 people works from Zurich and Lausanne with Swiss and international companies. Our work covers AI strategy and governance, data transformation and AI use cases that run in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing: Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner to take over and grow Artefact’s commercial business in Lausanne. The office already serves clients across Romandie, and its Tech chapter is led by a Partner on site. You will take over an established client portfolio and grow it against ambitious targets: deepen existing relationships, win new accounts in industry, retail and luxury, and grow the team that delivers them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your role will encompass:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking over existing client relationships in Romandie through a structured handover, and growing them into broader, multi-year partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opening new accounts with business leaders (CEO, COO, CMO, Chief Digital Officer, heads of business units) at industrial, retail, consumer and luxury companies in Romandie, and at the regional headquarters of international groups around Lake Geneva.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing Artefact’s Lausanne office with the Swiss Managing Partner and our Lausanne Tech Partner: more clients, more revenue and a larger team. You will also strengthen Artefact’s visibility in the French-speaking business and academic ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading client executives through data and AI transformation, so that Artefact becomes their partner of choice for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Among your responsibilities as Partner, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop the Romandie client portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run an account and go-to-market plan for Romandie: growth targets for existing clients, new target accounts and entry offers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your pipeline and report on it monthly: qualified opportunities, conversion rate, sold revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write proposals that address the client’s actual problem, own scoping and pricing, and shape them with the Tech chapter so that strategy and implementation come as one offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand existing accounts to more buyers and business units per client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver to the highest standard&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sponsor engagements run day to day by Engagement Managers, with multidisciplinary teams of consultants, data scientists and data/AI engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for client satisfaction, project margin and team experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop our knowledge base&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a sector edge in industry, retail or luxury: where data and AI change margins, operations or customer experience, and how to package that into offers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speak and publish in French and English on data and AI topics relevant to these sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Artefact’s global industry practices to bring their assets and references to Swiss clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the Lausanne team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow the Lausanne team with Swiss leadership through hiring and internal development, and own staffing on your engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach consultants on client handling, problem solving and sector knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12–15 years of experience, mostly in consulting: technology consulting, strategy consulting, transaction services/due diligence, or a large consulting and technology services firm. A move in-house after a consulting career is welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently Director, Principal or Associate Partner with a personal sales target, ready for the step to Partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing client relationships: you can name accounts you expanded and the revenue you sold, including clients you opened yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sector experience in industrial goods, retail, consumer or luxury, and a network among decision-makers in Romandie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French at native or full professional level, and fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency in data and AI: you can discuss what an AI use case needs from data, what it costs and when it pays back, without being an engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or willing to relocate to the Lausanne area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape what comes next: the Swiss practice has proven itself and is growing fast. It is still small enough that you shape its clients, its offers and its team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell with a global platform: you bring the credentials, delivery capacity and AI assets of a 2,500-person firm into every proposal, and you work with industry leads across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy to production under one roof: our consultants and engineers work in the same teams, so your clients get from recommendation to working solution without changing firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture: innovation, collaboration and action shape how we work. Artefact Switzerland is Great Place to Work certified (2026).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurship: you are measured on the clients, revenue and team you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/artefact/consulting-partner-romandie-strategy-data-ai-transformation-lausanne-vaud-138562","tags":["Data Consulting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Lausanne, Vaud","created_at":1791914111},{"slug":"consulting-partner-in-pharma-life-science-strategy-data-ai-transformation-zurich-463014","company_name":"Artefact","title":"Consulting Partner in Pharma & Life Science (Strategy & Data/AI Transformation)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a global data and AI consulting firm. We help organisations turn data and AI into measurable business impact across the value chain, from strategy and operating model to data platforms, AI products and marketing. More than 2,500 consultants, data scientists and engineers work for over 1,000 clients worldwide, including Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Switzerland, our team of around 50 people works from Zurich and Lausanne with Swiss and international companies. Our work covers AI strategy and governance, data transformation and AI use cases that run in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing: Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner to scale Artefact’s Pharma &amp;amp; Life Sciences practice in Switzerland. Many global pharma, biotech and medtech companies run their headquarters, R&amp;amp;D, manufacturing or commercial functions from Switzerland. We already work with life sciences clients here and now want to make this practice one of the pillars of our Swiss business. This is an origination role: most of your time goes into winning new clients and expanding existing relationships. You will be based in Zurich and work with clients across Basel, Zurich and Romandie.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your role will encompass:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
