efining the capabilities required to address validated needs, balancing improvements, new functionality and technology evolution, and communicating priorities across relevant teams.</p><p>• Develop business cases and commercial input by defining success measures and commercial objectives, providing evidence for portfolio investment decisions, and supporting Product Marketing with product knowledge for pricing and launch readiness.</p><p>• Coordinate the product core team by working with System Engineering on requirements and feasibility, Product Ownership on executable increments, and Project Management on customer delivery, while aligning Sales, Business Development, Customer Projects and Engineering around progress, quality and outcomes.</p> <br> <p>• Master’s degree in engineering or design, or equivalent experience.</p><p>• 5+ years of experience in Software Product Management, with a proven track record of developing, deploying and maintaining software (platform) driven solutions in defense industry or another industrial high-tech / high compliance environment</p><p>• Strong understanding of software products, particularly in complex and regulated environments, e.g., industrial environments.</p><p>• In-depth knowledge of software product management and – strategy methodologies.</p><p>• Demonstratable experience in defining software product strategy and creating complete business cases.</p><p>• Strong cross-functional leadership and stakeholder management skills at operational and management level</p><p>• Demonstrated critical thinking, adaptability to challenges, and a problem-solving mindset to creatively address user pain points.</p><p>• Proficiency in software industry standard tooling for software development and road mapping such as Jira / Jira Product Discovery / Jira Service Management, Confluence, BigPicture</p><p>• Excellent verbal and written communication skills, capable of conveying product level knowledge, decisions and roadmaps to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p><p>• Willingness to travel</p><p>• Drivers’ license B (or international equivalent)<br><br></p><p><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><p>• Experience in defense industry or another industrial high-tech / high compliance environment</p><p>• Proficiency in JAMA Connect, Siemens Polarion, SAFe, Miro, Figma, Dovetail, Amplitude, PowerBI</p><p>• Proficiency in Dutch language is a plus</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Security screening</strong></p><p>You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please check: </p><p>https://english.aivd.nl/topics/s/security-screening</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-product-manager-software-amsterdam-168851","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792009953},{"slug":"senior-customer-experience-designer-amsterdam-98992","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Customer Experience Designer","description":"<p><strong>About Optics11</strong></p><p>Optics11 is a fast-growing high-tech company based in Amsterdam, developing advanced fiber optic sensing systems for the most demanding environments. Our technology detects the earliest signs of failure in critical assets – from high-voltage energy infrastructure to subsea and defense applications – and gives our customers precise, real-time data they can act on.<br><br></p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p>As Senior Customer Experience Designer you will build a deep understanding of the use of both our hardware and software we supply to our defense partn